# libretranslate
msgid "**AI assistance inside the applications you already run.** A gateway role, *svc-ai-litellm*, fronts OpenAI, Anthropic and OpenRouter from declared keys, with *svc-ai-ollama* and the new *svc-ai-lmstudio* serving local models from one shared catalogue, so inference can stay inside the deployment. Sixteen applications use it for their own built-in AI features instead of calling a vendor directly: WordPress AI Engine, MediaWiki AIEditingAssistant, Moodle's AI subsystem, Zammad Smart Assist, the xWiki LLM extension, Discourse AI, the Matrix ChatGPT bridge, Nextcloud, Mattermost Agents, n8n, Open WebUI and Flowise. The gateway's admin UI signs in through Keycloak. See [svc-ai-litellm](roles/svc-ai-litellm/README.md) and [svc-ai-lmstudio](roles/svc-ai-lmstudio/README.md)."
msgstr "**AAren laguntza exekutatzen ari zaren aplikazioetan.** Atebidearen papera, *svc-ai-litellm*Aurrean OpenAI, Anthropic eta OpenRouter, gako deklaratuetatik, *svc-ai-ollama* eta berria *svc-ai-lmstudio* Eredu lokalak katalogo partekatu batetik zerbitzatuz, inferentzia hedapenaren barruan gera daiteke. Hamasei aplikaziok erabiltzen dute AAko ezaugarri propioetarako, saltzaileari zuzenean deitu ordez: WordPress AI Engine, MediaWiki Laguntzailea, MoodleAA azpisistema, Zammad Smart Assist, xWiki LLM hedapena, Discourse AI, Matrix ChatGPT zubia, Nextcloud, Mattermost Agenteak, n8n, Open WebUI eta Flowise. Atebideko administratzailearen UI seinaleak sartzen dira Keycloak. [svc-ai-litellm](roles/svc-ai-litellm/README.md) eta [svc-ai-lmstudio](roles/svc-ai-lmstudio/README.md)."

