# libretranslate
msgid "**An agent can be provisioned with its own platform user account.** Creating an agent employee optionally provisions a dedicated identity through the platform's existing user mechanism (the `users` lookup, LDAP via [`svc-db-openldap`](../../roles/svc-db-openldap/), SSO via [`web-app-keycloak`](../../roles/web-app-keycloak/)); no new account system is built. The account is a **non-privileged standard user** by default (never administrator/service-account-with-mutating-tools). When enabled, the agent authenticates as its own user: OIDC login to its dashboard, a distinct mailbox/identity, and MCP calls made with `auth_subject: user` ([025](025-mcp-role-integration.md)) scoped to that account rather than a shared service account. The account is opt-in per agent; its password/token lives in the role's `meta/secrets.yml` `credentials:` block, never in README or env. An agent MUST also be deployable against an existing account (no forced account creation)."
msgstr "**Agente bat bere plataformako erabiltzaile-kontuarekin eman daiteke.** Agente bat sortzeak aukera ematen du nortasun dedikatua plataformaren erabiltzaile mekanismoaren bidez. (eta `users` bilaketa, LDAP bidez [`svc-db-openldap`](../../roles/svc-db-openldap/), SSO via [`web-app-keycloak`](../../roles/web-app-keycloak/))Ez dago kontu-sistema berririk. Kontua da **Erabiltzaile estandar pribilegiatua** lehenespenez (inoiz ez administratzaile/zerbitzu-tresna trukagarriak)Gaituta dagoenean, agenteak bere erabiltzaile gisa autentifikatuko du: OIDC bere arbelera, postontzi/identitate ezberdinera, eta MCPk egindako deiak. `auth_subject: user` ([025](025-mcp-role-integration.md)) Kontu horren barruan, zerbitzu-kontu partekatu baten ordez. Kontua agente bakoitzeko opt-in da; bere pasahitza/tokena paperaren parte da `meta/secrets.yml` `credentials:` Blokea, inoiz ere ez README edo env-ean. Agente bat lehendik dagoen kontu baten aurka ere zabaldu behar da (kontu beharturik sortu gabe)."

# libretranslate
msgid "**An engine inside its consumer's project** — matrix with its own postgres, for instance — is started service by service rather than as a whole project, because bringing the project up would start the consumer and the chain refuses to replay while one runs. The discriminator is the dump's volume name against its project name: equal for the central engines (`postgres` in project `postgres`), different for a per-app one (`matrix_database` in project `matrix`)."
msgstr "**Motorra bere kontsumitzailearen proiektuaren barruan** - Matrizea bere postgres propioarekin, adibidez, zerbitzuz hasten da proiektu osoa baino, zeren eta proiektua aurrera eramateak kontsumitzailea abiaraziko luke eta kateak ez du berriro jokatu nahi. Diskriminatzailea dump-aren bolumenaren izena da proiektuaren izenaren aurka: motor zentralen berdina (`postgres` proiektuan `postgres`), desberdina aplikazio bakoitzeko (`matrix_database` proiektuan `matrix`)."

