# libretranslate
msgid "**MCP client contract:** With Home Assistant deployed, the role declares the MCP client side of the platform contract as an internal streamable-HTTP client with a read-only tool policy. The MCP server list itself lives in `openclaw.json`, not in the container environment."
msgstr "**MCP bezeroaren kontratua:** Zurekin Home Assistant Zabalduta, MCPren bezeroa plataforma-kontratuaren alderdia barne-korronte-HTTP bezero gisa adierazten du, irakurtzeko soilik den tresna-politikarekin. MCP zerbitzarien zerrenda bertan bizi da `openclaw.json`, Ez edukiontzi-ingurunean."

# libretranslate
msgid "**MCP client contract:** With an MCP server deployed alongside it, the role declares the MCP client side of the platform contract as an internal streamable-HTTP client with a read-only tool policy. The deploy registers every discovered provider in the instance-level `/api/v1/custom-mcp-servers` registry under an `infinito:` name, stores the bearer as an encrypted `CUSTOM_HEADERS` `authConfig`, authorizes each entry and compares the discovered tools against the provider's declared allowlist. `CUSTOM_MCP_PROTOCOL=sse` pins the deployment to URL-based MCP servers, so no flow can spawn a local stdio command. Reaching an MCP server whose URL resolves inside the container network requires `HTTP_SECURITY_CHECK=false` plus an `HTTP_DENY_LIST` that keeps loopback and the cloud-metadata addresses denied; both are rendered only while MCP servers are discovered, and the deploy proves the list is live by pointing a throwaway entry at each denied address. One managed Agentflow fixture calls a single named tool with fixed arguments and is executed on every deploy. Wiring a provider into a flow of your own stays an operator step."
msgstr "**MCP bezeroaren kontratua:** MCP zerbitzari bat bere ondoan jarrita, rolak adierazten du plataforma-kontratuaren MCP bezeroa barneko HTTP bezeroa dela, irakurtzeko soilik den tresna-politikarekin. Hedadurak aurkituriko hornitzaile guztiak erregistratzen ditu instantzia mailan `/api/v1/custom-mcp-servers` erregistro baten azpian `infinito:` izena, eramailea enkriptatuta gordetzen du `CUSTOM_HEADERS` `authConfig`, sarrera bakoitza baimentzen du eta hornitzailearen baimen-zerrenda deklaratuaren aurkako aurkitutako tresnak konparatzen ditu. `CUSTOM_MCP_PROTOCOL=sse` URLan oinarritutako MCP zerbitzarietara hedatzea ezartzen du, beraz, ez da fluxurik egongo tokiko stdio komandorik. MCP zerbitzari batera iritsi eta bere URLak edukiontzi-sarearen barruan erabakitzen du. `HTTP_SECURITY_CHECK=false` plus bat `HTTP_DENY_LIST` begizta eta hodei-metadatuen helbideak ukatu egiten dira; biak MCP zerbitzariak aurkitu bitartean ematen dira, eta deployak frogatzen du zerrenda bizirik dagoela, ukatutako helbide bakoitzean sarrera bat seinalatuz. Kudeatutako Agentflow batek argumentu finkoak dituen tresna bakar bat deitzen du eta hedapen bakoitzean exekutatzen da. Hornitzaile bat zure kabuz fluxura eramateak eragilearen urrats bat ematen du."

# libretranslate
msgid "**MCP client contract:** With an MCP server deployed alongside it, the role declares the MCP client side of the platform contract as an internal streamable-HTTP client with a read-only tool policy. The deploy registers every discovered provider in the instance-level ``/api/v1/custom-mcp-servers`` registry under an ``infinito:`` name, stores the bearer as an encrypted ``CUSTOM_HEADERS`` ``authConfig``, authorizes each entry and compares the discovered tools against the provider’s declared allowlist. ``CUSTOM_MCP_PROTOCOL=sse`` pins the deployment to URL-based MCP servers, so no flow can spawn a local stdio command. Reaching an MCP server whose URL resolves inside the container network requires ``HTTP_SECURITY_CHECK=false`` plus an ``HTTP_DENY_LIST`` that keeps loopback and the cloud-metadata addresses denied; both are rendered only while MCP servers are discovered, and the deploy proves the list is live by pointing a throwaway entry at each denied address. One managed Agentflow fixture calls a single named tool with fixed arguments and is executed on every deploy. Wiring a provider into a flow of your own stays an operator step."
