# libretranslate
msgid "**Test notes.** The RBAC tiers are proven by moving ``biber`` through the groups with LAM’s Multi edit tool and asserting both the grant and the revoke, rather than by dedicated accounts. ``/ui/vault/logout`` does not end a session — the Ember app restores its token from browser storage — so use the UI’s own logout control when the session must actually be gone."
msgstr "**Probako oharrak.** RBAC fitxak mugitzen direla frogatuta daude ``biber`` LAM-en Multi edizio-tresna duten taldeen bidez eta bai beka eta bai erreboka baieztatuz, kontu dedikatuen bidez baino. ``/ui/vault/logout`` Ez da saioa amaitzen: Anbar aplikazioak arakatzailearen biltegitik tokena berreskuratzen du; beraz, erabili UIren kontrol-saioa amaitu behar denean."

# libretranslate
msgid "**Test notes.** The RBAC tiers are proven by moving `biber` through the groups with LAM's Multi edit tool and asserting both the grant and the revoke, rather than by dedicated accounts. `/ui/vault/logout` does not end a session — the Ember app restores its token from browser storage — so use the UI's own logout control when the session must actually be gone."
msgstr "**Probako oharrak.** RBAC fitxak mugitzen direla frogatuta daude `biber` LAM-en Multi edizio-tresna duten taldeen bidez eta bai beka eta bai erreboka baieztatuz, kontu dedikatuen bidez baino. `/ui/vault/logout` Ez da saioa amaitzen: Anbar aplikazioak arakatzailearen biltegitik tokena berreskuratzen du; beraz, erabili UIren kontrol saioa amaitu behar denean."

# libretranslate
msgid "**Testing and documentation tooling.** New *test-e2e-cli* exercises the command-line interface end to end. Lint and test jobs publish per-target and per-test summaries, failed target logs are replayed after the summary, and the complexity matrix shows whether a role already exists on *origin/main*. Generated role READMEs now provide consistent status tables, quick-start instructions and dependency diagrams."
msgstr "**Probak eta dokumentazio-tresnak.** Berria *test-e2e-cli* komando-lerroaren interfazea amaitzen da. Lint eta probako lanak argitaratzen ditu per-target eta per-test laburpenak, huts egindako helburuko erregistroak laburpenaren ondoren erreproduzitzen dira, eta konplexutasun-matrizeak erakusten du rol bat existitzen den edo ez. *jatorria/nagusia*READMEs-ek orain egoera-taula koherenteak, hasierako argibideak eta mendekotasun-diagramak eskaintzen ditu."

# libretranslate
msgid "**Tests in every language the project ships.** The quality gate parses each shipped language and runs its unit suite; the PHP and Ruby interpreters are baked into the image, and the JavaScript, PHP and Ruby suites are reported in the CI summary alongside Python. Playwright stages the persona flows once per run and mounts them read-only, and the workspace environment suite splits into base, compose and swarm tracks."
msgstr "**Hizkuntza guztietan probatzen du proiektuak.** Kalitate-ateak itzulitako hizkuntza bakoitza aztertzen du eta unitate-suitea exekutatzen du; PHP eta Ruby interpretatzaileak irudian egosten dira, eta JavaScript, PHP eta Ruby suiteak CIren laburpenan ematen dira Python-en ondoan. Playwright-ek pertsona bat behin korrika egiten du eta irakurtzeko soilik muntatzen ditu, eta laneko arearen inguruneko suitea oinarrietan banatzen da, pistak konposatu eta pilatzen ditu."

# libretranslate
msgid "**The UI is published, the MCP surface is not.** *(Revised during implementation; the original decision was internal-only for both.)* Home Assistant follows the `web-app-*` contract and serves its own UI on a canonical domain through the reverse proxy, because every part of that contract — `meta/domains.yml`, `meta/csp.yml`, the guest Playwright persona — assumes a public vhost, and a role without one would have to be shaped as a `svc-*` role instead. The hub's own auth provider guards that surface. The MCP endpoint stays `exposure: internal`: it is reachable in-cluster only, an unauthenticated probe of the public origin is refused, and `files/playwright/test-mcp-guest.js` asserts exactly that. A platform-SSO gate in front of the UI remains a documented follow-up."
msgstr "**UIa argitaratuta dago, MCPren azalera ez.** *(Inplementazioan errebokatua; jatorrizko erabakia barnekoa zen bientzat.)* Home Assistant ondoren `web-app-*` kontratua eta bere UIa eskaintzen du domeinu kanoniko batean alderantzizko proxy-aren bidez, kontratuaren zati bakoitza- `meta/domains.yml`, `meta/csp.yml`, Playwright persona gonbidatuak ostatu publiko bat hartzen du bere gain, eta rol bat gabe moldatu beharko litzateke. `svc-*` Paperaren ordez. hub-aren auth-hornitzaileak gainazal hori zaintzen du. MCPren amaiera-puntua hemen dago `exposure: internal`: distirara soilik iristen da, jatorri publikoko zunda bat ukatu egiten da, eta `files/playwright/test-mcp-guest.js` Hori baieztatzen du. UIren aurrean dagoen plataforma-SSO ate batek jarraipena egiten jarraitzen du."

msgid "**The ``mcp`` role is granted per platform, not per application.** A user’s ``roles:`` list carries role names only, and ```build_realm_rbac_groups`` <../web-app-keycloak/filter_plugins/build_realm_rbac_groups.py>`__ matches them without an application context, so ``roles: [mcp]`` makes that user a member of *every* deployed ``/roles/<app>/mcp`` group. Entitling somebody to drive Baserow but not GitLab is therefore not expressible declaratively today; it needs the Keycloak membership to be set directly on the single group. The tool-server side honours whatever membership arrives, so the limit is the platform’s user model, not this wiring, and the Playwright coverage reflects it: it proves “all groups sees all servers” and “no group sees none”, not the selective case."
msgstr ""

# libretranslate
msgid "**The `mcp` role is granted per platform, not per application.** A user's `roles:` list carries role names only, and [`build_realm_rbac_groups`](../web-app-keycloak/filter_plugins/build_realm_rbac_groups.py) matches them without an application context, so `roles: [mcp]` makes that user a member of *every* deployed `/roles/<app>/mcp` group. Entitling somebody to drive Baserow but not GitLab is therefore not expressible declaratively today; it needs the Keycloak membership to be set directly on the single group. The tool-server side honours whatever membership arrives, so the limit is the platform's user model, not this wiring, and the Playwright coverage reflects it: it proves \"all groups sees all servers\" and \"no group sees none\", not the selective case."
msgstr "**The `mcp` Rola plataformako ematen da, ez aplikazioko.** Erabiltzaile baten izena `roles:` Zerrendak rol-izenak bakarrik ditu, eta [`build_realm_rbac_groups`](../web-app-keycloak/filter_plugins/build_realm_rbac_groups.py) aplikazio-testuingururik gabe bat datoz. `roles: [mcp]` erabiltzaile horrek kide egiten du *bakoitza* hedatua `/roles/<app>/mcp` taldea. Baserow gidatzeko norbait bultzatzea, baina ez GitLab, beraz, ez da gaur egun argi eta garbi azaltzen; Keycloak-eko kide izatea behar du talde bakarrean zuzenean ezartzeko. Tresna-zerbitzariak edozein kideri ohore egiten dio, beraz, muga plataformaren erabiltzaile-eredua da, ez hariketa hori, eta Playwright-en estaldurak islatzen du: \"talde guztiek zerbitzari guztiak ikusten dituzte\" eta \"inork ez du ikusten\"Ez kasu selektiboa."

# libretranslate
msgid "**The agent then runs autonomously, step by step:**"
msgstr "**Orduan, agenteak modu autonomoan egiten du lan, urratsez urrats:**"

msgid "**The alias is the switch.** `services.litellm.router_alias` defaults to `auto`; setting it empty publishes no route and renders no `callbacks` entry, so the hook is not even a condition of starting the proxy. One knob, because a separate enable flag would let `services.yml` read as on while the router is off."
msgstr ""

# libretranslate
msgid "**The app volumes are really discarded** (`down --volumes`) and re-created empty by `compose create`, so what comes back can only come from the backup. The database projects go down without `--volumes` on purpose: their data directory carries the database itself, which the deploy creates and the container does not, so a wiped datadir would leave `baudolo-restore --empty -d <db>` with nothing to connect to. The database half loses no proof by it — the pre-clean drops the schema including the marker table, and only the dump brings it back."
msgstr "**Aplikazioaren bolumenak baztertu egiten dira.** (`down --volumes`) eta berriro sortu zen hutsik `compose create`, Itzultzen dena babeskopiatik bakarrik etor daiteke. Datu-basearen proiektuak jaitsi egiten dira. `--volumes` helburuz: datu-direktorioak datu-basea bera du, eta horrek sortzen du eta edukiontziak ez, beraz, ezabatutako datu-dir batek utziko luke. `baudolo-restore --empty -d <db>` Ezerekin konektatzeko. Datu-basearen erdiak ez du inolako frogarik galtzen; pre-garbiak eskema bertan behera uzten du, markatzaileen taula barne, eta dump-ak bakarrik itzultzen du."

# libretranslate
msgid "**The axes are part of a row's identity.** They appear in the job label as glyphs, in the plan table as columns, and in the artifact name. Two rows that differ only in distro are two deploys and MUST NOT share an artifact name."
msgstr "**Ardatzak errenkada baten identitatearen zati dira.** Lan-etiketan glyphs gisa agertzen dira, plan-taulan zutabe gisa, eta objektu-izenean. Distroan bakarrik bereizten diren bi errenkada bi biderketa dira eta ez dute izen artifizialik partekatu behar."

# libretranslate
#, python-format
msgid "**The axes are selectable.** `%distro` and `/filesystem` narrow a `whitelist` or `priority` token the same way `@mode` and `+tor` do. A retrigger reads the distro back off a failed job's title, so a red row returns on the distribution it died on. It does not read the filesystem back: the title states the kind the matrix assigned, which a deploy may have fallen back from, and writing it into a token would state it as named by a human and make it binding."
msgstr "**Ardatzak hautagarriak dira.** `%distro` eta `/filesystem` estua `whitelist` edo `priority` token berdin `@mode` eta `+tor` Egizu. Atzera-grabatzaile batek huts egindako lanaren titulua irakurtzen du, eta, beraz, errenkada gorri bat itzultzen da hil zen banaketan. Ez du fitxategi-sistema atzera irakurtzen: tituluak adierazten du zein matrize-motari esleitu zaion, zeinetatik adats bat erori den, eta token batean idazteak gizaki batek izendatu eta lotuko luke."

# libretranslate
msgid "**The consumers must be down.** `--empty` pre-cleans the schema in one psql session and replays in the next; a booting consumer recreates the schema in between and the dump's own `CREATE TABLE` then fails. The replay checks the consumer's compose project and refuses while anything of it runs."
msgstr "**Kontsumitzaileak jaitsi egin behar dira.** `--empty` eskema psql saio batean garbitu eta hurrengo batean jokatzen du; kontsumitzaile abioko batek eskema birsortzen du eta irauliaren berarena. `CREATE TABLE` gero huts egiten du. Erreproduzitzeak kontsumitzailearen konposaketa-proiektua egiaztatzen du, eta uko egiten dio ezer gertatzen den bitartean."

# libretranslate
msgid "**The consumers must be down.** ``--empty`` pre-cleans the schema in one psql session and replays in the next; a booting consumer recreates the schema in between and the dump’s own ``CREATE TABLE`` then fails. The replay checks the consumer’s compose project and refuses while anything of it runs."
msgstr "**Kontsumitzaileak jaitsi egin behar dira.** ``--empty`` eskema psql saio batean garbitu eta hurrengo batean jokatzen du; abio-kontsumitzaile batek eskema birsortzen du eta zabortegiaren berarena. ``CREATE TABLE`` gero huts egiten du. Erreproduzitzeak kontsumitzailearen konposaketa-proiektua egiaztatzen du, eta uko egiten dio ezer gertatzen den bitartean."

msgid "**The decision is deterministic, and a learned decision model is out of scope.** Among the routes that survive the filter, each is scored on the factors of decision 9 and the highest scorer wins, with the alias breaking a tie. The same request therefore returns the same model twice. No inference runs, nothing is downloaded, and the CI rows mean the same thing as production."
msgstr ""

# libretranslate
msgid "**The deploy can create a role-internal administrator.** On an instance with no users at all there is no OIDC administrator to borrow an API key from, so [`tasks/utils/mcp.yml`](./tasks/utils/mcp.yml) creates the `openwebui-api-bot` declared in [`meta/users.yml`](./meta/users.yml), whose password the platform generates with every other user's. It is deliberately not an OIDC identity: Open WebUI ships `OAUTH_MERGE_ACCOUNTS_BY_EMAIL` disabled and refuses an OIDC login whose email a local account already holds, so seeding a person's address would lock them out of their own login. On an instance that already has an administrator no account is created."
msgstr "**Hedapenak rol barneko administratzaile bat sor dezake.** Kasu batean, erabiltzailerik gabe, ez dago OIDC administratzailerik API gako bat maileguan hartzeko. [`tasks/utils/mcp.yml`](./tasks/utils/mcp.yml) sortzen du `openwebui-api-bot` deklaratuta [`meta/users.yml`](./meta/users.yml), Plataformak beste erabiltzaile guztiekin sortzen duen pasahitza. Ez da nahita OIDC identitatea: Open WebUI ontziak `OAUTH_MERGE_ACCOUNTS_BY_EMAIL` desgaituta eta uko egiten dio OIDC-ren saio-hasiera bati, kontu lokal batek jadanik duen posta elektronikoari, beraz, pertsona baten helbideak bere saio-hasieratik blokeatuko lituzke. Dagoeneko administratzaile bat duen kasu batean ez da konturik sortzen."

# libretranslate
msgid "**The deploy can create a role-internal administrator.** On an instance with no users at all there is no OIDC administrator to borrow an API key from, so ```tasks/utils/mcp.yml`` <./tasks/utils/mcp.yml>`__ creates the ``openwebui-api-bot`` declared in ```meta/users.yml`` <./meta/users.yml>`__, whose password the platform generates with every other user’s. It is deliberately not an OIDC identity: Open WebUI ships ``OAUTH_MERGE_ACCOUNTS_BY_EMAIL`` disabled and refuses an OIDC login whose email a local account already holds, so seeding a person’s address would lock them out of their own login. On an instance that already has an administrator no account is created."
msgstr "**Hedapenak rol barneko administratzaile bat sor dezake.** Kasu batean, erabiltzailerik gabe, ez dago OIDC administratzailerik API gako bat maileguan hartzeko. ```tasks/utils/mcp.yml`` <./tasks/utils/mcp.yml>`__ creates the ``openwebui-api-bot`` declared in ```meta/users.yml`` <./meta/users.yml>`__, whose password the platform generates with every other user’s. It is deliberately not an OIDC identity: Open WebUI ships ``OAUTH_MERGE_ACCOUNTS_BY_EMAIL`` desgaituta eta uko egiten dio OIDC-ren saio-hasiera bati, kontu lokal batek jadanik duen posta elektronikoari, beraz, pertsona baten helbideak bere saio-hasieratik blokeatuko lituzke. Dagoeneko administratzaile bat duen kasu batean ez da konturik sortzen."

# libretranslate
msgid "**The engine is read, not guessed.** It comes from the service key in the consuming role's `meta/services.yml`, the same value that fed the backup seed, resolved through `utils/recovery/databases.py`. A dump whose engine no role claims aborts the run instead of being replayed with an assumption."
msgstr "**Motorra irakurria dago, ez asmatua.** Zerbitzu-gakotik dator, kontsumo-funtzioan. `meta/services.yml`, Babeskopia-hazia elikatzen zuen balio bera. `utils/recovery/databases.py`. Hondakin bat, zeinaren motorrak ez duen inolako betebeharrik, exekuzioa bertan behera uzten duen, suposizio baten ordez."

# libretranslate
msgid "**The engine is read, not guessed.** It comes from the service key in the consuming role’s ``meta/services.yml``, the same value that fed the backup seed, resolved through ``utils/recovery/databases.py``. A dump whose engine no role claims aborts the run instead of being replayed with an assumption."
msgstr "**Motorra irakurria dago, ez asmatua.** Zerbitzu-gakotik dator, kontsumo-funtzioan. ``meta/services.yml``, Babeskopia-hazia elikatzen zuen balio bera. ``utils/recovery/databases.py``. Hondakin bat, zeinaren motorrak ez duen inolako betebeharrik, exekuzioa bertan behera uzten duen, suposizio baten ordez."

# libretranslate
msgid "**The file's content IS the value of `applications.<app>.<topic>`. There is NO wrapping key matching the filename.**"
msgstr "**Fitxategiaren edukia balioa da `applications.<app>.<topic>`. Ez dago fitxategi-izenarekin bat datorren bilgarri-gakorik.**"

# libretranslate
msgid "**The gateway is authenticated with per-consumer virtual keys.** LiteLLM virtual keys are issued per consumer (OpenWebUI, Flowise, and each 032 agent); a master key is admin-only. This gives per-consumer rate limiting and revocation. The gateway MUST NOT be reachable unauthenticated even on the internal overlay. Keys live in each consumer role's `meta/secrets.yml` `credentials:` block."
msgstr "**Sarbidea gako birtualekin autentifikatuta dago.** LiteLLM gako birtualak kontsumitzaile bakoitzeko igortzen dira (OpenWebUI, Flowise eta bakoitza 032 agentea); Gako nagusia administratzea da soilik. Honek kontsumo-tasaren mugapena eta errebokatzea ematen du. Atebidea ez da atez atekoa izan behar barneko gainjartzean ere. Gakoak kontsumitzaile bakoitzaren funtzioetan bizi dira `meta/secrets.yml` `credentials:` blokea."

# libretranslate
msgid "**The head leads unless an operator says otherwise.** Chunk 0 starts at the top of the ranking. The list is ordered coverage-first, so its head is what a run most needs proven, and a sweep that cannot afford the whole list leaves the tail behind rather than sliding a window over it."
msgstr "**Buruak gidatuko du, operadoreak bestela esaten ez badu.** Chunk 0 rankingaren goialdean hasten da. Zerrenda estaldura ordenatua da lehenik, beraz, bere burua da beharrik gehien erakutsi duena, eta zerrenda osoa ordaindu ezin duen miaketa batek isatsa uzten du leiho bat gainetik irristatu ordez."

msgid "**The hook ships as a mounted Python file, not a derived image.** LiteLLM's `proxy_server.py` resolves a custom handler through `get_instance_fn(value, config_file_path)`, which loads `module.instance` out of the directory holding `config.yaml`. A `.py` file rendered next to it is therefore imported at proxy start with no image change, and `services.litellm.image` stays on its pin. [`probe_auth.py`](../../roles/svc-ai-litellm/files/python/probe_auth.py) is the precedent for a Python file the role ships and the container runs."
msgstr ""

# libretranslate
msgid "**The integration matrix is a generated artifact with a sanctioned generator.** The generator lives under `cli/build/docs/integration_matrix/` and runs through `make integration-matrix`; `docs/` holds only the rendered page. It MUST satisfy the repo lints: its `EDGES` data moves into a sibling data module so the entrypoint stays under the 500-line limit, it uses the shared project-root helper instead of a local `__file__` upward walk, and it carries no self-path literal or `requirement NNN` token. The generated `027-integration-matrix.md` carries a `generated-artifact / not-a-requirement` head marker so the requirements-completeness/archival lint skips it. Dead upstream URLs in `EDGES` are fixed or dropped on regeneration."
msgstr "**Integrazio-matrizea sortu den artefaktu bat da, sorgailu zigortu batekin.** Sorgailua azpian bizi da `cli/build/docs/integration_matrix/` eta korrika `make integration-matrix`; `docs/` Errendatutako orria bakarrik dauka. Errepontsak bete behar ditu: `EDGES` datuak bikoizketa-modulu batean sartzen dira, beraz sarrera-puntua azpian geratzen da. 500-lerro-muga, proiektu-errendimendu partekatua erabiltzen du tokiko laguntzaren ordez. `__file__` Gora doa, eta ez du auto-bide literalik, ez `requirement NNN` token. Sortua `027-integration-matrix.md` eraman `generated-artifact / not-a-requirement` buru-markatzaileak, beraz, eskakizunen betetasuna/artxibaleko lintak saltatu egiten du. Gora-beherako URLak `EDGES` konponduak edo birsorkuntzan eroriak."

# libretranslate
msgid "**The integration matrix is the cross-role addon backlog.** The full role×role capability map lives in the generated companion [027-integration-matrix.md](027-integration-matrix.md) (source of truth: [cli/build/docs/integration_matrix](../../cli/build/docs/integration_matrix/__main__.py)). ☑️ cells are integrations **already wired** through an infinito-native service flag in the row role's `meta/services.yml` (e.g. `sso`→keycloak, `matomo`, `prometheus`, `email`→mailu), derived by scanning the repo, no action required. ✅ cells are verified **upstream app↔app plugins not yet declared** as addons, the backlog this requirement commits to wire. 🪙 cells are the same as ✅ but gated behind a commercial tier (opt-in, operator-enabled). ❌ cells have no known integration. The matrix MUST be regenerated (not hand-edited) whenever a role or an integration is added; the `meta/addons/` migrations turn ✅ into ☑️ over time."
msgstr "**Integrazio-matrizea alderantzizko barra-barra da.** Rol-xrole-gaitasunen mapa osoa sortzen duen lagunarengan bizi da [027-integrazioa...matrix.md](027-integration-matrix.md) (Egiaren iturria: [cli/build/docs/integration_matrix](../../cli/build/docs/integration_matrix/__main__.py)). ☑️ zelulak integrazioak dira **dagoeneko kableatua** bandera mugagabe baten bidez, ilara-rolean. `meta/services.yml` (Adibidez: `sso`→keycloak, `matomo`, `prometheus`, `email`→mailu)Errepoa eskaneatzearen ondorioz, ez da ekintzarik behar. ✅ Gelaxkak egiaztatuta daude **upstream aplikazioen pluginak oraindik ez dira aitortu** addons gisa, baldintza hau alanbreari dagokio. 🪙 zelulak berdinak dira ✅ baina maila komertzial baten atzean makurtuta (opt-in, eragilea gaituta). ❌ gelaxkek ez dute integraziorik ezagutzen. Matrizea berriro sortu behar da (eskuz editatu gabe) Rol bat edo integrazio bat gehitzen den bakoitzean, `meta/addons/` migrazioak datoz ✅ sartu ☑️ Denborarekin."

# libretranslate
msgid "**The job proves the machine before it deploys.** [assert_architecture.sh](../../../scripts/github/runner/assert_architecture.sh) compares `uname -m` against the assigned value and fails the row on a mismatch. Without it, a label that stops resolving to arm64 hardware would report every arm64 row green from an amd64 machine, which is the exact failure the axis exists to rule out."
msgstr "**Lanak makina frogatzen du hedatu aurretik.** [assert_architecture.sh](../../../scripts/github/runner/assert_architecture.sh) konparazioak `uname -m` esleitutako balioaren aurka eta errenkada ez dator bat. Hori gabe, besotik kentzeari uzten dion etiketa64 hardwareak beso guztien berri ematen du64 berdea amd batetik64 makina, hau da, ardatzaren hutsegite zehatza."

# libretranslate
msgid "**The matrix carries the runner label, and `runs-on` reads it.** The entry gains `architecture` and `runner`; [pools.py](../../../utils/github/variant/pools.py) owns the mapping (`amd64` → `ubuntu-latest`, `arm64` → `ubuntu-24.04-arm`). An architecture without a label is a build error rather than a row that lands on the wrong hardware with an empty `runs-on`."
msgstr "**Matrizeak korrikalariaren etiketa darama, eta `runs-on` irakurri.** Sarrerak irabazten du `architecture` eta `runner`; [pools.py](../../../utils/github/variant/pools.py) mapaketaren jabea da (`amd64` → `ubuntu-latest`, `arm64` → `ubuntu-24.04-arm`)Etiketarik gabeko arkitektura eraikuntza-errorea da, okerreko hardwarean hutsik dagoen errenkada bat baino. `runs-on`."

# libretranslate
msgid "**The migration is blocked on a transport gap, and the credential half of it is already built.** The adapter presented its upstream credential only as a header (`ADAPTER_UPSTREAM_KEY` → `Authorization: Bearer …`) while Baserow keys its endpoint by URL segment, so `policy.upstream_url` now splices an optional `ADAPTER_UPSTREAM_PATH_KEY` and `ADAPTER_UPSTREAM_PATH_SUFFIX` into the upstream URL, delivered through the same `upstream.env` file. With neither variable set it returns the base URL unchanged, which is why the fourteen existing providers are untouched."
msgstr "**Migrazioa blokeatuta dago garraio-hutsune batean, eta kredentzialaren erdia egina dago jadanik.** Egokitzaileak bere korrontearen kredentziala goiburu gisa bakarrik aurkeztu zuen. (`ADAPTER_UPSTREAM_KEY` → `Authorization: Bearer …`) Baserow-k bere amaierako puntua URL segmentuaren bidez ezartzen duen bitartean, beraz, `policy.upstream_url` orain aukerako bat ematen du `ADAPTER_UPSTREAM_PATH_KEY` eta `ADAPTER_UPSTREAM_PATH_SUFFIX` igotako URLra, bide beretik bidalita `upstream.env` fitxategia. Aldagai-multzorik gabe, oinarrizko URLa itzultzen du aldatu gabe, eta horregatik daude hamalau hornitzaileak ukitu gabe."

# libretranslate
msgid "**The pools are narrowable per run.** The `distros` and `filesystem` inputs default to empty, which means every declared value. Narrowing is for chasing one distribution or one filesystem."
msgstr "**Igerilekuak estugarriak dira korrikako.** The `distros` eta `filesystem` sarrera hutsak, balio deklaratu guztiak esan nahi du. Narrowing banaketa edo fitxategi-sistema baten atzetik ibiltzea da."

# libretranslate
msgid "**The raft volume is `nfs: false` and the service carries `placement: manager`.**"
msgstr "**Baltsaren bolumena da `nfs: false` eta zerbitzuak eramaten du `placement: manager`.**"

# libretranslate
msgid "**The recovery key is the way back in.** ``bao operator init`` issues it once and nothing reissues it, which is what makes it useful — it is the only authority here that does not rotate. It is persisted through ``sys-token-store`` (``DIR_SECRETS``, backed up, and it survives both ``MODE_RESET`` and a replaced manager, each of which takes ``.applied.json`` with it). When neither the inventory AppRole nor the recorded one is accepted, ``tasks/utils/recover.yml`` mints a root token from it and re-pins the AppRole. It cannot decrypt the store — only the seal key can — so it is not a substitute for backing up the inventory."
msgstr "**Berreskuratze-gakoa da itzultzeko modua.** ``bao operator init`` behin eta berriz errepikatzen du, eta horrek balio du: hemen ez da biratzen duen autoritate bakarra. irauten du ``sys-token-store`` (``DIR_SECRETS``, eta biak bizirik irauten du. ``MODE_RESET`` eta ordezko kudeatzailea, bakoitzak berea ``.applied.json`` honekin). Inbentarioa eta grabatua onartzen ez direnean, ``tasks/utils/recover.yml`` Erroko token bat moztu eta AppRole berriro birjartzen du. Ezin du biltegia desenkriptatu, zigiluak bakarrik egin dezake, beraz ez da inbentarioaren ordezkoa."

# libretranslate
msgid "**The recovery key is the way back in.** `bao operator init` issues it once and nothing reissues it, which is what makes it useful — it is the only authority here that does not rotate. It is persisted through `sys-token-store` (`DIR_SECRETS`, backed up, and it survives both `MODE_RESET` and a replaced manager, each of which takes `.applied.json` with it). When neither the inventory AppRole nor the recorded one is accepted, `tasks/utils/recover.yml` mints a root token from it and re-pins the AppRole. It cannot decrypt the store — only the seal key can — so it is not a substitute for backing up the inventory."
