msgid "A Tor node's resolv.conf names only the local dnsmasq, so probing its entries alone cannot say whether the pinned upstream was still alive when that dnsmasq went silent. Anything unreadable or keyless yields []."
msgstr "Tor nodo bat resolv.conf Bertako dnsmasq izena bakarrik du, beraz, bere sarrerak aztertzeak ez du esan nahi oraindik bizirik zegoenik dnsmasq hori isildu zenean. Ezer irakurtezina edo funtsezkorik gabea. []."

# libretranslate
msgid "A `## Cosmos` section MUST contain a single Mermaid `flowchart` that places the role in the Infinito.Nexus cosmos. Group the nodes with `subgraph`s into three families:"
msgstr "A `## Cosmos` atal batek sirena bakarra eduki behar du `flowchart` horrek jartzen du papera Infinito.Nexus Kosmosa. Elkartu nodoak honekin `subgraph`Hiru familiatan:"

# libretranslate
msgid "A `Dockerfile.j2` with **Jinja2 control-flow logic** emits a **warning only**. The warning signals that the file should be reviewed to see whether the logic can be eliminated and the file migrated."
msgstr "A `Dockerfile.j2` honekin: **Jinja2 kontrol-fluxuaren logika** igortzen du a **abisua soilik**Abisuak adierazten du fitxategia berrikusi behar dela logika ezabatu eta fitxategia migratu ahal izateko."

# libretranslate
msgid "A `Dockerfile.j2` with **no Jinja2 control-flow logic** causes a **test failure**. It MUST be migrated to `files/Dockerfile` with `ARG` declarations."
msgstr "A `Dockerfile.j2` honekin: **Jinjarik ez2 kontrol-fluxuaren logika** a **proba-hutsegitea**migratu egin behar da `files/Dockerfile` honekin: `ARG` Adierazpenak."

# libretranslate
msgid "A `SYSTEM_EMAIL_<KEY>` variable defined in inventory, group vars, or host vars. No such file ships with the project. This form is an escape hatch for site-specific overrides."
msgstr "A `SYSTEM_EMAIL_<KEY>` Inbentarioan, talde-aldaketetan edo ostalari-aldaketetan definitutako aldagaia. Ez dago horrelako fitxategi-ontzirik proiektuarekin. Forma hau ihes-ate bat da gune zehatzetarako."

# libretranslate
msgid "A ``database = '*'`` row dumps a whole instance with ``pg_dumpall``. It goes back through ``baudolo-restore cluster`` with the instance's superuser; its ``\\connect`` lines name the databases, while the consumers sit in the compose project of the engine, so both are checked."
msgstr "A ``database = '*'`` errenkadak instantzia osoa isurtzen du ``pg_dumpall``. Berriro pasatzen da ``baudolo-restore cluster`` adibidearen gainerabiltzailearekin; ``\\connect`` lerroek datu-baseak izendatzen dituzte, kontsumitzaileak motorraren konposaketa-proiektuan esertzen diren bitartean, beraz, biak dira egiaztatzaileak."

# libretranslate
msgid "A ``host_gateway`` upstream resolves through ``host.docker.internal`` in ``/etc/hosts`` (host gateway), which the request-time ``resolver`` cannot see, so it renders as a literal directive like compose."
msgstr "A ``host_gateway`` Upstream-en bidez ebazten da ``host.docker.internal`` barruan ``/etc/hosts`` (ostalariaren atebidea), eta eskaera-ordua ``resolver`` Ezin da ikusi, beraz, konposaketa bezalako direktiba literala da."

# libretranslate
msgid "A ``maxmemory`` ceiling derived from the service ``mem_limit`` with an ``allkeys-lru`` policy."
msgstr "A ``maxmemory`` zerbitzutik datorren sabaia ``mem_limit`` batekin ``allkeys-lru`` politika."

# libretranslate
msgid "A ``mount --make-rshared /`` runs once in the deploy container before the runner starts, because MDAD’s systemd units bind-mount ``/matrix/synapse/storage`` with ``bind-propagation=slave``, which requires shared/slave propagation on the source."
msgstr "A ``mount --make-rshared /`` behin exekutatzen da deploy edukiontzian korrikalaria hasi aurretik, MDADen unitate sistematuak muntatzen dituelako ``/matrix/synapse/storage`` honekin: ``bind-propagation=slave``, eta horrek esklabutza partekatua behar du iturrian."

# libretranslate
msgid "A ``svc-bkp-*`` pre-backup hook for ``bench backup`` is NOT wired in v1 (deferred to a follow-up requirement). The v1 backup story relies on the standard ``svc-bkp-*`` driver picking up the central MariaDB DB and the role’s named volumes. To make a Frappe-aware snapshot in flight, run:"
msgstr "A ``svc-bkp-*`` aurreko kakorako ``bench backup`` Ez dago haririk v-an1 (Jarraipen-eskakizun batera atzeratuta). v1 babeskopiaren historia estandarran oinarritzen da ``svc-bkp-*`` Gidariak MariaDB DB zentrala eta paperaren bolumenak jasotzen ditu. Frappe-aware baten argazkiak ateratzeko, egin lasterka:"

# libretranslate
msgid "A ``type: volume`` entry may set ``nfs: false`` to opt out of the swarm NFS rewrite: the volume then stays a plain node-local named volume even when ``storage.backend`` is ``nfs`` (e.g. gitaly repository storage, which upstream forbids on NFS). Any other ``nfs`` value (absent, ``true``, or the uid/gid/mode dict consumed by the NFS subdir pre-creation) keeps the rewrite."
msgstr "A ``type: volume`` Sarrera ezar daiteke ``nfs: false`` NFS berridazketa-multzotik kanpo uzteko: bolumena nodo lokal izendatutako bolumen soila izaten jarraitzen du, nahiz eta ``storage.backend`` da ``nfs`` (adibidez, biltegien biltegia, NFSk debekatu egiten duena). Beste edozein ``nfs`` balioa (ausentzia, ``true``, edo uid/gid/mode NFS subdir aurre-sorkuntzak kontsumitutako diktua) berriro idazten jarraitzen du."

# libretranslate
msgid "A `deprecated` role:"
msgstr "A `deprecated` Rola:"

# libretranslate
msgid "A `maxmemory` ceiling derived from the service `mem_limit` with an `allkeys-lru` policy."
msgstr "A `maxmemory` zerbitzutik datorren sabaia `mem_limit` batekin `allkeys-lru` politika."

# libretranslate
msgid "A `mount --make-rshared /` runs once in the deploy container before the runner starts, because MDAD's systemd units bind-mount `/matrix/synapse/storage` with `bind-propagation=slave`, which requires shared/slave propagation on the source."
msgstr "A `mount --make-rshared /` behin exekutatzen da deploy edukiontzian korrikalaria hasi aurretik, MDADen unitate sistematuak muntatzen dituelako `/matrix/synapse/storage` honekin: `bind-propagation=slave`, eta horrek esklabutza partekatua behar du iturrian."

# libretranslate
msgid "A `required: false` addon whose install step fails MUST register the failure, emit a warning (role log line plus, in CI, a GitHub Actions warning annotation via `utils.annotations.message.warning`), skip the addon's remaining steps, and let the play continue."
msgstr "A `required: false` instalazio-urratsak huts egiten badu, hutsegitea erregistratu behar du, abisu bat eman (Rol-lerro bat gehi, CI-n, GitHub-eko ekintzak abisu-abisuaren bidez `utils.annotations.message.warning`), saltatu addonaren gainerako urratsak, eta utzi jokoari."

# libretranslate
msgid "A `required: true` addon whose install step fails MUST fail the play (no `failed_when: false` swallowing the error)."
msgstr "A `required: true` instalazio-urratsak huts egiten duen gehigarria (ez `failed_when: false` Errorea irentsiz)."

# libretranslate
msgid "A `required_by` block MAY instead nest `compose:` / `swarm:` sub-blocks to scope the requirement to one deploy mode (a flat block applies in every mode); the deploy mode is inferred from the role set (swarm pulls in svc-swarm-node):"
msgstr "A `required_by` blokearen ordez habia `compose:` / `swarm:` azpi-blokeak eskaera modu bat zabaltzeko (Bloke laua modu guztietan aplikatzen da); deploy modua esleitutako funtziotik inferitzen da (svc-swarm-node):"

# libretranslate
msgid "A `svc-bkp-*` pre-backup hook for `bench backup` is NOT wired in v1 (deferred to a follow-up requirement). The v1 backup story relies on the standard `svc-bkp-*` driver picking up the central MariaDB DB and the role's named volumes. To make a Frappe-aware snapshot in flight, run:"
msgstr "A `svc-bkp-*` aurreko kakorako `bench backup` Ez dago haririk v-an1 (Jarraipen-eskakizun batera atzeratuta). v1 babeskopiaren historia estandarran oinarritzen da `svc-bkp-*` Gidariak MariaDB DB zentrala eta paperaren bolumenak jasotzen ditu. Frappe-aware baten argazkiak ateratzeko, egin lasterka:"

# libretranslate
msgid "A `templates/Dockerfile.j2` is acceptable when the file contains Jinja2 control-flow logic that cannot be expressed through Docker `ARG` alone, for example a conditional build step that installs an optional component only when a feature flag is enabled."
msgstr "A `templates/Dockerfile.j2` onargarria da fitxategiak Jinja duenean2 Docker-en bidez adierazi ezin den kontrol-fluxuaren logika `ARG` bakarrik, adibidez, aukerako osagai bat instalatzen duen baldintza-eraikitze-urrats bat eginbide-bandera gaituta dagoenean bakarrik."

# libretranslate
msgid "A `v*` tag push fans out into two CI workflows:"
msgstr "A `v*` etiketatu jarraitzaileak CIren bi lan-fluxutan:"

# libretranslate
msgid "A bare `mode=update` without `variant=` on a matrix-variant role. Every `mode=update` MUST carry `variant=<idx>` (row 2). A missing `variant=` is never a reason to switch to `mode=reinstall`."
msgstr "A hutsa `mode=update` gabe `variant=` Matrize-bariante batean. Denak `mode=update` Eraman egin behar da `variant=<idx>` (errenkada 2). Falta den bat `variant=` inoiz ez da arrazoia aldatzeko `mode=reinstall`."

# libretranslate
#, python-brace-format
msgid "A bare list is shorthand for ``{names: [...], source: repo}``. An empty list states that the package is deliberately not installed on that family, which counts as covered; a *missing* key is a coverage gap."
msgstr "Zerrenda huts bat laburra da ``{names: [...], source: repo}``. Zerrenda huts batek dio paketea ez dagoela nahita instalatuta familia horretan, estalita dagoen moduan. *falta da* Gakoa estaldura-hutsune bat da."

# libretranslate
msgid "A bare role name loses to any token that narrows the same row: writing ``role role#1@swarm`` asks for a specific deploy, not for that deploy plus a rotation-picked one on top."
msgstr "Rol-izen soil batek errenkada bera estutzen duen edozein token galtzen du: idaztea ``role role#1@swarm`` Desabantaila zehatz bat eskatzen du, ez zabaltze hori, ezta biraketa bat ere."

# libretranslate
msgid "A bare run id resolves owner/repo from ``repo_override`` or the current gh repo."
msgstr "Exekutatzeko ID biluzi batek jabea/errepoa ebazten du ``repo_override`` edo uneko gh repo."

# libretranslate
msgid "A baseline deploy for `<role>` completed successfully in the current environment."
msgstr "Oinarrizko hedapena `<role>` Ongi burutu da uneko ingurunean."

# libretranslate
msgid "A bind on `127.0.0.1:5672` plus the shared cross-stack overlay network for consumers."
msgstr "Lotu bat `127.0.0.1:5672` gainjarritako sare partekatua kontsumitzaileentzat."

# libretranslate
msgid "A bind on `127.0.0.1:6379` plus the shared cross-stack overlay network for consumers."
msgstr "Lotu bat `127.0.0.1:6379` gainjarritako sare partekatua kontsumitzaileentzat."

# libretranslate
msgid "A bind on ``127.0.0.1:5672`` plus the shared cross-stack overlay network for consumers."
msgstr "Lotu bat ``127.0.0.1:5672`` gainjarritako sare partekatua kontsumitzaileentzat."

# libretranslate
msgid "A bind on ``127.0.0.1:6379`` plus the shared cross-stack overlay network for consumers."
msgstr "Lotu bat ``127.0.0.1:6379`` gainjarritako sare partekatua kontsumitzaileentzat."

# libretranslate
msgid "A blank ``current`` (the addon tracks the app default) never produces a suggestion, and a non-semver ``latest`` is ignored so the checker never proposes a non-comparable tag."
msgstr "Hutsik ``current`` (addon-ek aplikazio lehenetsia jarraitzen du) inoiz ez da iradokizunik egiten, eta ez-semver bat. ``latest`` Ez zaio jaramonik egiten, beraz, egiaztatzaileak ez du etiketa banagarririk proposatzen."

# libretranslate
msgid "A block device (remote path under ``/dev/``) is recovered on the host over ssh (the host must carry the repo checkout), then the restored backup tree is rsync-pulled. An image file is rsync-pulled and recovered locally. Either way the result is a local backup root the caller then recovers from."
msgstr "Bloke-gailua (urruneko bidearen azpian ``/dev/``) ostalarian ssh bidez berreskuratu da (ostalariak repo checkout-a eraman behar du)Beraz, berreskuratutako babeskopia-zuhaitza erretxina da. Irudi-fitxategi bat erretxina da eta lokalki berreskuratzen da. Edozein modutan, emaitza babeskopia lokalaren erro bat da, deitzaileak berreskuratu egiten du."

# libretranslate
msgid "A block naming a key the entity does not carry, or a type the resolver does not know, would otherwise pin nothing and say nothing."
msgstr "Entitateak eramaten ez duen gako bat izendatzen duen bloke batek, edo ebazleak ez dakienak, bestela ez luke ezer esango."

# libretranslate
msgid "A block that only one side has is usually a feature the other never had. Check whether it was superseded before dropping it — grep for its variables."
msgstr "Alde batek bakarrik duen blokea, normalean, besteak izan ez duen ezaugarria da. Begiratu ea gainditua izan den, utzi aurretik, bere aldagaiengatik."

# libretranslate
msgid "A body that asserts only constants (`expect(1).toBe(1)`) without driving any role surface is rejected on review."
msgstr "Konstanteak soilik baieztatzen dituen gorputz bat (`expect(1).toBe(1)`) Rol-azalik gidatu gabe, berrikuspena ez da onartzen."

# libretranslate
msgid "A body that carries a `TODO`, `STUB`, `FIXME`, or `XXX` marker is rejected. The contract requires real flows, not deferred work."
msgstr "Gorputz bat daramana `TODO`, `STUB`, `FIXME`, edo `XXX` Ezetsita dago markatzailea. Kontratuak fluxu errealak behar ditu, ez atzeratutako lanak."

# libretranslate
msgid "A body that contains only `skipUnlessServiceEnabled(...)` (or any combination of helper calls) without at least one `expect(...)`, `await <fn>(...)`, or equivalent real-flow step is rejected."
msgstr "Soilik daukan gorputz bat `skipUnlessServiceEnabled(...)` (edo laguntza-deien konbinazioren bat) bat ere ez `expect(...)`, `await <fn>(...)`, edo fluxu errealaren urrats baliokidea ez da onartzen."

# libretranslate
msgid "A branch is ready to be opened as a pull request"
msgstr "Adar bat irekitzeko prest dago tira-eskaera gisa"

# libretranslate
msgid "A bridged service block MUST carry the standard `enabled` / `shared` flags so requirement 019 (services.yml parity) and the SSO/LDAP coverage requirements (017, 018) continue to apply unchanged."
msgstr "Zubiztatutako zerbitzu-bloke batek estandarra eraman behar du `enabled` / `shared` banderak baldintza gisa 019 (services.yml paritatea) eta SSO/LDAPen estaldura baldintzak (017, 018) Jarraitu aldatzen."

# libretranslate
msgid "A built-in (embedded) runner executes tasks in the main container; external `semaphore runner` agents are optional for scale-out."
msgstr "Inkorporatua (kapsulatua) korrikalariak atazak exekutatzen ditu edukiontzi nagusian; kanpokoak `semaphore runner` Agenteak eskalatzeko aukerakoak dira."

# libretranslate
msgid "A built-in ``rabbitmq-diagnostics ping`` healthcheck."
msgstr "Inkorporatua ``rabbitmq-diagnostics ping`` Osasun-egiaztapena."

# libretranslate
msgid "A built-in `rabbitmq-diagnostics ping` healthcheck."
msgstr "Inkorporatua `rabbitmq-diagnostics ping` Osasun-egiaztapena."

# libretranslate
msgid "A bulleted list of the most important capabilities. Each item MUST start with a **bold** label followed by a colon and a short explanation."
msgstr "Gaitasun garrantzitsuenen zerrenda. Elementu bakoitza a batekin hasi behar da **ausarta** Ondoren bi puntu eta azalpen labur bat."

# libretranslate
msgid "A candidate the curated relevance rules reject is silently dropped so broad marketplaces never produce unreviewable noise."
msgstr "Garrantziaren arau sendagarriak baztertzen dituen hautagaia merkatu zabaletan inoiz ez da zarata ikustezina sortzen."

msgid "A capability neither catalogued nor declared counts as absent, and a limit neither catalogued nor declared is not enforced."
msgstr ""

# libretranslate
msgid "A change is incompatible with prior inventories, on-disk role-meta layout, deploy CLI, or stored runtime state."
msgstr "Aldaketa bat bateraezina da aurreko inbentarioekin, diskoko paper-meta diseinuarekin, CLI hedatuz edo gordetako exekuzio-egoerarekin."

msgid "A changed source becomes an empty entry, a removed source disappears."
msgstr ""

# libretranslate
msgid "A classic personal access token MAY be used as a fallback for unrelated automation, but it MUST NOT be used here because user-bound credentials expand the blast radius and require manual rotation."
msgstr "Sarbide pertsonal klasikoko token bat automatizazioarekin zerikusia ez duen atzeraldi gisa erabil daiteke, baina ez da hemen erabili behar, erabiltzaileak ezarritako kredentzialek leherketa-erradioa zabaltzen dutelako eta eskuzko biraketa behar dutelako."

# libretranslate
msgid "A clean `down && up` is required after the change: `make compose-up` alone recreates the bridge but compose then re-attaches existing containers with dynamic IPs instead of the static `default.env` ones, which breaks CoreDNS."
msgstr "Garbia `down && up` Aldaketaren ondoren beharrezkoa da: `make compose-up` zubia bakarrik birsortzen du, baina ondoren dauden edukiontziak berriro gehitzen ditu IP dinamikoekin estatikoaren ordez. `default.env` CoreDNS hausten dutenak."

# libretranslate
msgid "A client MUST NOT treat an unreachable provider as fatal while the play is still running. Roles deploy in dependency order, so a client that probes during its own role can run before a provider exists at all, and aborting there prevents that provider from ever deploying. This is the same exemption `credential_missing` already carries, and it ends the same way: the reconciliation stage probes with `MCP_RECONCILE_STRICT` once every provider has run, and a provider still unreachable there is a real failure."
msgstr "Bezero batek ez du hornitzaile atziezina hilgarritzat hartu behar jokoa oraindik martxan dagoen bitartean. Rolak mendekotasun-ordenan hedatzen dira, beraz, bezero batek, bere eginkizunan proba egiten badu, hornitzaile bat sortu aurretik exekutatu ahal izango du, eta bertan behera uzteak hornitzailea inoiz ez erabiltzea eragozten du. Hau salbuespen bera da `credential_missing` Dagoeneko eramaten du, eta berdin amaitzen du: adiskidetze-eszena proben bidez `MCP_RECONCILE_STRICT` hornitzaile guztiak korrika egin ondoren, hornitzaile bat oraindik ez da atzigarri, hutsegite bat dago."

# libretranslate
msgid "A client declares what it can present instead of what it serves:"
msgstr "Bezero batek adierazten du zer aurkez dezakeen, zerbitzatzen duenaren ordez:"

# libretranslate
msgid "A client role discovers enabled shared server roles through the lookup, resolves the per-server credential, then connects server-to-server to each `/mcp` endpoint over Streamable HTTP. No candidate list is hard-coded and no browser-side fetch is involved."
msgstr "Bezero-rol batek zerbitzari partekatuen funtzioak aurkitzen ditu bilaketaren bidez, zerbitzariko kredentziala ebazten du, eta zerbitzaritik zerbitzarira konektatzen du bakoitza. `/mcp` HTTP korrontearen amaierako puntua. Ez dago hautagaien zerrendarik kodetuta eta ez dago arakatzailearen aldeko mezurik."

# libretranslate
msgid "A client-only block MUST NOT declare an `endpoint`."
msgstr "Bezeroentzako bakarrik den bloke batek EZ du deklaratu behar `endpoint`."

msgid "A closing bracket that moves in front of a protected span takes the full stop behind it with it, which leaves the sentence running on."
msgstr ""

# libretranslate
msgid "A cluster row states the cluster marker where a single-database row names a database, so :func:`credentials_of` would file every instance under the same key and keep only the first. Cluster credentials are therefore keyed by instance."
msgstr "klusterreko errenkada batek klusterraren markatzailea adierazten du, datu-base bakarreko errenkadak datu-base bat izendatzen duen lekua, beraz :func:`credentials_of` instantzia guztiak gako beraren pean jarriko lituzke eta lehena bakarrik mantenduko luke. Klusterraren kredentzialak, beraz, kasuaren arabera gakotzen dira."

msgid "A cold server answers its opening requests well above its steady rate, and the pair measured first used to inherit that and win every sweep. Repeating a pair back to back does not help, because all of its runs then sit inside the same opening window. The grid is therefore walked once per pass and the passes are what repeat, so the bonus lands on one run of one pair and the median drops it. The recorded spread says whether the winner is a real difference or the noise the whole grid sits in."
msgstr ""

# libretranslate
msgid "A colon suffix on `<source>` is classified by shape:"
msgstr "Bi puntuko atzizkia `<source>` formaren arabera sailkatzen da:"

# libretranslate
msgid "A complete digital learning environment for schools, academies, and universities."
msgstr "Ikasteko ingurune digital osoa ikastetxe, akademia eta unibertsitateentzat."

# libretranslate
msgid "A computed fallback defined in `_compute(short_key, resolved, variables)`."
msgstr "Kalkulatutako atzerakada bat definitua `_compute(short_key, resolved, variables)`."

# libretranslate
msgid "A concrete end-to-end illustration of how the pieces compose. Nothing here is a new mechanism; it maps onto the decisions above."
msgstr "Piezak nola osatzen diren erakusten duen ilustrazio zehatza. Hemen ezer ez da mekanismo berria, goiko erabakietara mapatzen du."

# libretranslate
msgid "A condition that makes the replay unprovable."
msgstr "Erreprobisa ezinezko bihurtzen duen baldintza."

# libretranslate
msgid "A confirmed hit is cached on disk. The probe stays on the upstream registry: it exists to prove the declared pin is still pullable from where the deploy pulls it, which a mirrored copy cannot answer for."
msgstr "Egiaztatutako hit bat diskoan gordetzen da. Zundak gora-beherako erregistroan jarraitzen du: deklaratutako pina oraindik tiragarria dela frogatzeko dago, deployak tira egiten duen lekutik, eta ispiludun kopia batek ezin du erantzun."

# libretranslate
msgid "A constant hides the role id the substring rule looks for, so every SPOT of this kind MUST be listed here or the roles referencing it silently drop their provider from the static closure."
msgstr "Etengabe ezkutatu egiten du azpikatearen erregelak bilatzen duen papera, eta, beraz, mota honetako SPOT guztiak zerrendatu behar dira hemen edo erreferentzia egiten duten rolek isil-isilik utzi behar dute hornitzailea itxiera estatikotik."

# libretranslate
msgid "A consumer is a deployed role whose merged config enables a shared database of the provider's engine; a role with a dedicated database brings its own volume and is no consumer of the provider. A provider without a consumer holds only the databases its engine creates for itself, so no databases.csv row names it and baudolo records its volume undumped."
msgstr "Kontsumitzailea funtzio hedatua da, eta konfigurazioak hornitzailearen motorraren datu-base partekatua gaitzen du; datu-base dedikatu batek bere bolumena ekartzen du eta ez da hornitzailearen kontsumitzailea. Kontsumitzailerik gabeko hornitzaile batek bere motorrak sortzen dituen datu-baseak bakarrik dauzka, beraz, ez databases.csv Errenkadak izena ematen dio eta baudolok bere bolumena ez da aldatu."

msgid "A consumer reaches it as ``http://searxng:8080/search?q=<query>`` once it declares ``searxng`` in its own ``meta/services.yml`` with ``enabled`` and ``shared`` set. ``web-app-openwebui`` ships that flag and sends ``WEB_SEARCH_ENGINE=searxng`` with it."
msgstr ""

msgid "A consumer reaches it as ``http://tika:9998`` once it declares ``tika`` in its own ``meta/services.yml`` with ``enabled`` and ``shared`` set, which is what attaches the consumer to this role’s network. ``web-app-openwebui`` ships that flag and sends ``CONTENT_EXTRACTION_ENGINE=tika`` with it."
msgstr ""

