# libretranslate
msgid "Amended after implementation: the deployed Hermes version serves a bearer API rather than a browser dashboard, so its native-OIDC support cannot be used. It is gated at the auth proxy instead, like OpenClaw and Flowise, admitting the role's `administrator` and `mcp` groups. Holding `API_SERVER_KEY` alone was the whole boundary before, which put every MCP provider Hermes is admitted to behind one shared deployment secret. The cost of the proxy is deliberate: an OpenAI-compatible client presenting only a bearer no longer reaches Hermes through its public vhost, and has to come from inside the container network."
msgstr "Inplementatu ondoren aldatua: hedatutako Hermes bertsioak API eramailea balio du arakatzailearen arbelaren ordez, eta beraz, ezin da erabili jatorrizko OIDC euskarria. Horren ordez, auth proxy-an dago, OpenClaw eta Flowise-n bezala, rol hori onartuz. `administrator` eta `mcp` taldeak. Eutsi `API_SERVER_KEY` Lehen muga osoa bakarrik zegoen, eta horrek Hermes MCPren hornitzaile guztiak hedapen partekatu baten atzean uzten ditu. Proxy-aren kostua nahita egiten da: bezero bateragarri bat, eroale bat bakarrik aurkezten duena, bere ostalari publikoaren bidez, eta edukiontzi-saretik etorri behar du."

# libretranslate
msgid "Among the hosts in `svc-swarm-node`, the cluster manager is identified by additional membership in `svc-swarm-manager`. v1 scope: exactly ONE host. Workers are derived as `svc-swarm-node − svc-swarm-manager` — no duplicated list in `group_vars`."
msgstr "Ostalarien artean `svc-swarm-node`, kluster-kudeatzailea kide gehiagoren bidez identifikatzen da `svc-swarm-manager`.1 Esparrua: ostalari bat. Langileak honela sortzen dira: `svc-swarm-node − svc-swarm-manager` - ez dago bikoiztutako zerrendarik `group_vars`."

