# libretranslate
msgid "Behind that sits a second, smaller mismatch. LAM authenticates by binding an LDAP DN from its `Admins` list, which [`templates/env.j2`](./templates/env.j2) fills with `LDAP.DN.ADMINISTRATOR.DATA` and `LDAP.BIND_CREDENTIAL` — the `svc-db-openldap` `credentials.administrator_database_password` — while the shared helper types `lookup('users', 'administrator').password`, the secret of `uid=administrator,ou=users,…`, a different directory entry. That one is configurable rather than structural: the helper reads `ADMIN_NATIVE_PASSWORD` for exactly this case, and the role could render it. It is recorded here so the opt-out can be revisited together with the entry-point problem, which is the blocking one."
msgstr "Horren atzean segundo bat dago, ez dator bat. LAM autentifikazioa LDAP DN bat beretik lotuz `Admins` zerrenda, zein [`templates/env.j2`](./templates/env.j2) beteak `LDAP.DN.ADMINISTRATOR.DATA` eta `LDAP.BIND_CREDENTIAL` - `svc-db-openldap` `credentials.administrator_database_password` -Laguntzaile partekatuak diren bitartean `lookup('users', 'administrator').password`, Sekretua `uid=administrator,ou=users,…`, Direktorioko beste sarrera bat. Hori konfiguragarria da egituraren ordez: laguntzaileak irakurtzen du `ADMIN_NATIVE_PASSWORD` Kasu honetan, hain zuzen ere, rolak errenda dezake. Hemen gordetzen da, aukera-irteera sarrera-puntuaren arazoarekin batera berraztertzeko, hau da, blokeoa."

# libretranslate
msgid "Behind that sits a second, smaller mismatch. LAM authenticates by binding an LDAP DN from its ``Admins`` list, which ```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__ fills with ``LDAP.DN.ADMINISTRATOR.DATA`` and ``LDAP.BIND_CREDENTIAL`` — the ``svc-db-openldap`` ``credentials.administrator_database_password`` — while the shared helper types ``lookup('users', 'administrator').password``, the secret of ``uid=administrator,ou=users,…``, a different directory entry. That one is configurable rather than structural: the helper reads ``ADMIN_NATIVE_PASSWORD`` for exactly this case, and the role could render it. It is recorded here so the opt-out can be revisited together with the entry-point problem, which is the blocking one."
msgstr "Horren atzean segundo bat dago, ez dator bat. LAM autentifikazioa LDAP DN bat beretik lotuz ``Admins`` zerrenda, zein ```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__ fills with ``LDAP.DN.ADMINISTRATOR.DATA`` and ``LDAP.BIND_CREDENTIAL`` — the ``svc-db-openldap`` ``credentials.administrator_database_password`` — while the shared helper types ``lookup('users', 'administrator').password``, the secret of ``uid=administrator,ou=users,…``, a different directory entry. That one is configurable rather than structural: the helper reads ``ADMIN_NATIVE_PASSWORD`` Kasu honetan, hain zuzen ere, rolak errenda dezake. Hemen gordetzen da, aukera-irteera sarrera-puntuaren arazoarekin batera berraztertzeko, hau da, blokeoa."

