# libretranslate
msgid "Snipe-IT is entered through a trusted-header bridge: the oauth2-proxy authenticates against Keycloak and Snipe-IT's `loginViaRemoteUser()` mints a native session for the matching `users.username` row (see [`files/php/apply/sso_config.php`](./files/php/apply/sso_config.php)). The gate declares no `allowed_groups`, so `biber` passes the proxy — but the role provisions only the administrator account ([`tasks/03_admin.yml`](./tasks/03_admin.yml)), so the header carries a username Snipe-IT does not know and the visitor falls back to the native login form. [`templates/playwright.env.j2`](./templates/playwright.env.j2) therefore declares `PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`, while the `administrator` persona stays live (`PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=false`) and exercises the full bridge end to end."
msgstr "Snipe-IT zubi fidagarri batetik sartzen da: oauth2-Autentifikatutako proxy-a Keycloak eta Snipe-IT-a `loginViaRemoteUser()` jatorrizko saio bat egiten du bat datorrenerako `users.username` errenkada (Ikusi [`files/php/apply/sso_config.php`](./files/php/apply/sso_config.php))Atak ezetz dio `allowed_groups`, Horrela `biber` proxy-a gainditzen du, baina administratzailearen kontua bakarrik. ([`tasks/03_admin.yml`](./tasks/03_admin.yml))Beraz, goiburuak Snipe-IT erabiltzaile-izena darama, ez daki eta bisitaria jatorrizko saio-hasierako formara itzultzen da. [`templates/playwright.env.j2`](./templates/playwright.env.j2) beraz, `PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`, bitartean `administrator` pertsona bizirik dago (`PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=false`) eta amaitzen den zubi osoa erabiltzen du."

# libretranslate
msgid "Snipe-IT is entered through a trusted-header bridge: the oauth2-proxy authenticates against Keycloak and Snipe-IT’s ``loginViaRemoteUser()`` mints a native session for the matching ``users.username`` row (see ```files/php/apply/sso_config.php`` <./files/php/apply/sso_config.php>`__). The gate declares no ``allowed_groups``, so ``biber`` passes the proxy — but the role provisions only the administrator account (```tasks/03_admin.yml`` <./tasks/03_admin.yml>`__), so the header carries a username Snipe-IT does not know and the visitor falls back to the native login form. ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ therefore declares ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true``, while the ``administrator`` persona stays live (``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=false``) and exercises the full bridge end to end."
msgstr "Snipe-IT zubi fidagarri batetik sartzen da: oauth2-Autentifikatutako proxy-a Keycloak eta Snipe-IT-a ``loginViaRemoteUser()`` jatorrizko saio bat egiten du bat datorrenerako ``users.username`` errenkada (Ikusi ```files/php/apply/sso_config.php`` <./files/php/apply/sso_config.php>`__). The gate declares no ``allowed_groups``, so ``biber`` passes the proxy — but the role provisions only the administrator account (```tasks/03_admin.yml`` <./tasks/03_admin.yml>`__), so the header carries a username Snipe-IT does not know and the visitor falls back to the native login form. ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ therefore declares ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true``, while the ``administrator`` persona stays live (``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=false``) eta amaitzen den zubi osoa erabiltzen du."

# libretranslate
msgid "Snipe‑IT is an open‑source asset management system designed to streamline hardware and software inventory tracking. This deployment provides an automated, containerized solution using Docker Compose, centralized MariaDB database integration, and secure, configurable environment settings, including robust SMTP email support and pending SAML authentication enhancements."
msgstr "Snipe‐IT kode irekiko aktiboen kudeaketa sistema bat da, hardware eta softwareen inbentarioen jarraipena errazteko diseinatua. Hedapen honek soluzio automatizatu eta edukiontzidun bat eskaintzen du, Docker Composezentralizatua MariaDB datu-basearen integrazioa eta ingurune seguru eta konfiguragarria, SMTP posta-laguntza sendoa eta SAML autentifikazio-hobekuntzak barne."

# libretranslate
msgid "So `meta/services.yml` MUST NOT have a top-level `services:` key wrapping its content. `meta/volumes.yml` MUST NOT have a top-level `volumes:` key, and the same rule applies to `meta/server.yml`, `meta/rbac.yml`, `meta/users.yml`, and `meta/info.yml`. The filename alone fixes the path prefix in the materialised application tree, which keeps consumer paths short and predictable (no redundant `compose.…` prefixes)."
msgstr "Beraz, `meta/services.yml` Ez da maila gorenekoa izan behar `services:` bere edukia betetzen duen gakoa. `meta/volumes.yml` Ez da maila gorenekoa izan behar `volumes:` gakoa, eta arau bera aplikatzen zaio `meta/server.yml`, `meta/rbac.yml`, `meta/users.yml`, eta `meta/info.yml`. Fitxategi-izenak bakarrik finkatzen du bide-izenen aurrizkia aplikazio-zuhaitz materializatuan, eta horrek kontsumo-bideak labur eta aurreikusgarri mantentzen ditu. (erredundanterik ez `compose.…` aurrizkiak)."

# libretranslate
msgid "So a conditional `\"{{ 'web-app-matomo' in group_names }}\"` edge pulls its provider into the static closure regardless of whether `web-app-matomo` is actually selected. The closure is the co-deploy superset."
msgstr "Beraz, baldintza bat `\"{{ 'web-app-matomo' in group_names }}\"` ertzak bere hornitzailea itxitura estatikora eramaten du, kontuan hartu gabe ea `web-app-matomo` Izan ere, hautatua da. Ixtea gainmultzoa da."

# libretranslate
#, python-brace-format
msgid "So the format is read from the workflow itself. Every input renders as one segment, ``<head><value> ``, where the head is the emoji the workflow's own ``format('🐧{0} ', …)`` prefixes the value with. An input holding its default renders no segment at all, so a title carries only what deviates — and an absent input means \"the workflow's default\", which is exactly what a retrigger should leave alone."
msgstr "Beraz, formatua laneko fluxutik bertatik irakurtzen da. Sarrera bakoitzak segmentu bat ematen du, ``<head><value> ``, non burua emojia den lan-fluxuaren berarena ``format('🐧{0} ', …)`` balioari aurrea hartzen dio. Sarrera lehenetsi bat edukitzeak ez du segmenturik ematen, beraz, tituluak desbideratzen duena baino ez du hartzen, eta sarrera faltak esan nahi du \"lan-fluxuaren lehenetsia\"Hori da, hain zuzen ere, itzultzaile batek bakarrik utzi beharko lukeena."

# libretranslate
