# libretranslate
msgid "Taiga redirects `/` to the public `/discover` showcase, which renders a bare Login link but not the OIDC entry point; only `/login` binds the SSO directive (see the note in [`files/playwright/_shared.js`](./files/playwright/_shared.js)). The shared personas always enter at the site root, so they can never reach Taiga's SSO button. Taiga's AngularJS shell additionally exposes logout only through `ng-click` / `tg-nav` / `ui-sref` directives, which the generic in-app logout helper cannot activate. [`templates/playwright.env.j2`](./templates/playwright.env.j2) therefore declares `PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true` and `PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true`; the equivalent journeys are driven by the role-local `test-login-oidc.js` and `test-login-native.js` specs, which enter at `/login` and log out through Taiga's own control."
msgstr "Taiga birbideratzeak `/` publikoarentzat `/discover` Erakustaldia, saio-hasierako esteka hutsa bihurtzen duena, baina ez OIDC sarrera-puntua; `/login` SSO direktiba lotzen du (Ikusi oharra hemen [`files/playwright/_shared.js`](./files/playwright/_shared.js)). Pertsona partekatuak beti sartzen dira gunearen erroan, inoiz ez iristeko. TaigaSSO botoia. Taiga-ren AngularJS shell-ak, gainera, saioa amaitutzat ematen du. `ng-click` / `tg-nav` / `ui-sref` Helbideak, sarrera-laguntzaile generikoak aktibatu ezin dituenak. [`templates/playwright.env.j2`](./templates/playwright.env.j2) beraz, `PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true` eta `PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true`; bide baliokideak role-local-ek gidatzen ditu. `test-login-oidc.js` eta `test-login-native.js` sartzen diren espezieak `/login` eta amaitu saioa TaigaBere buruaren kontrola."

# libretranslate
msgid "Taiga redirects ``/`` to the public ``/discover`` showcase, which renders a bare Login link but not the OIDC entry point; only ``/login`` binds the SSO directive (see the note in ```files/playwright/_shared.js`` <./files/playwright/_shared.js>`__). The shared personas always enter at the site root, so they can never reach Taiga’s SSO button. Taiga’s AngularJS shell additionally exposes logout only through ``ng-click`` / ``tg-nav`` / ``ui-sref`` directives, which the generic in-app logout helper cannot activate. ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ therefore declares ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` and ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true``; the equivalent journeys are driven by the role-local ``test-login-oidc.js`` and ``test-login-native.js`` specs, which enter at ``/login`` and log out through Taiga’s own control."
msgstr "Taiga birbideratzeak ``/`` publikoarentzat ``/discover`` Erakustaldia, saio-hasierako esteka hutsa bihurtzen duena, baina ez OIDC sarrera-puntua; ``/login`` SSO direktiba lotzen du (Ikusi oharra hemen ```files/playwright/_shared.js`` <./files/playwright/_shared.js>`__). The shared personas always enter at the site root, so they can never reach Taiga’s SSO button. Taiga’s AngularJS shell additionally exposes logout only through ``ng-click`` / ``tg-nav`` / ``ui-sref`` directives, which the generic in-app logout helper cannot activate. ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ therefore declares ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` and ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true``; the equivalent journeys are driven by the role-local ``test-login-oidc.js`` and ``test-login-native.js`` specs, which enter at ``/login`` eta amaitu saioa TaigaBere buruaren kontrola."

# libretranslate
msgid "Tailored for Arch Linux, this role handles the installation of Firefox using the system’s package manager (``pacman``). It deploys a ``policies.json`` file to Firefox’s distribution directory, ensuring that critical extensions are automatically installed via Firefox Enterprise Policies."
msgstr "Arch Linux-erako egokitua, rol honek kudeatzen du instalazioa. Firefox sistemaren pakete-kudeatzailea erabiliz (``pacman``). A zabaltzen du ``policies.json`` fitxategia Firefoxbanaketa-direktorioa, hedapen kritikoak automatikoki instalatzen direla ziurtatuz Firefox Enpresa politikak."

# libretranslate
msgid "Tailored for Arch Linux, this role handles the installation of Firefox using the system’s package manager (`pacman`). It deploys a `policies.json` file to Firefox’s distribution directory, ensuring that critical extensions are automatically installed via Firefox Enterprise Policies."
