# libretranslate
msgid "The [per-role meta layout](../contributing/design/role/services/layout.md) already lists `addons`, `plugins`, and `modules` among the keys *inlined* under the primary service entity. This requirement promotes that concept to a first-class, per-file `meta/addons/<addon_id>.yml` topic (one file per addon, file root IS the addon spec), the same move requirement 011 made for `meta/info.yml` and requirement 008/009 made for other meta topics."
msgstr "The [meta-diseinua](../contributing/design/role/services/layout.md) zerrenda `addons`, `plugins`, eta `modules` gakoen artean *azpimarratua* Lehen mailako zerbitzu-erakundearen pean. Baldintza honek kontzeptu hori lehen mailakoa da, fitxategikoa. `meta/addons/<addon_id>.yml` gaia (fitxategi bat addon bakoitzeko, fitxategien erroa addon spec da)Mugitzeko baldintza bera 011 egina `meta/info.yml` eta baldintza 008/009 Beste gai batzuetarako egina."

# libretranslate
msgid "The `.onion` is a **deploy-time input**: a CLI helper mints the v3 key offline during inventory build, vaults it, and sets `DOMAIN_PRIMARY`. It must NOT be a runtime fact — `DOMAIN_PRIMARY` is consumed at build time (LDAP base, CA, applications cache). The role restores the minted key into the hidden-service volume before Tor starts."
msgstr "The `.onion` a **denbora-sarrera**: CLI-ren laguntzaileak v-a txikitzen du3 gakoa lineaz kanpo inbentarioaren eraikuntzan, ganga eta multzoan `DOMAIN_PRIMARY`-Ez da denbora-kontua izango... `DOMAIN_PRIMARY` eraikitzeko garaian kontsumitzen da (LDAP basea, CA, aplikazioen cachea). Rolak ezkutuko zerbitzuko bolumena berreskuratzen du Tor hasi aurretik."

# libretranslate
msgid "The `@playwright/test` version pinned into the rendered `package.json` comes from `playwright.version` in `roles/test-e2e-playwright/meta/services.yml` via the `image_version` filter. That YAML value is the single source of truth for the Playwright version."
msgstr "The `@playwright/test` bertsioa errendazioan itsatsia `package.json` dator `playwright.version` barruan `roles/test-e2e-playwright/meta/services.yml` bidez `image_version` iragazkia. YAML balioa Playwright bertsiorako egiaren iturri bakarra dela."

# libretranslate
msgid "The `API.cloudflare.api_token` value (declared in `group_vars/all/18_api.yml`, read via `lookup('api', 'cloudflare.api_token')`) must contain a valid Cloudflare API Token.   This token is used for all DNS operations and ACME (SSL/TLS certificate) challenges that require access to your Cloudflare-managed domains."
msgstr "The `API.cloudflare.api_token` balioa (deklaratuta `group_vars/all/18_api.yml`, irakurri bidez `lookup('api', 'cloudflare.api_token')`) Cloudflare baliozko bat eduki behar du API Token. token hau DNS eta ACME eragiketetan erabiltzen da (SSL/TLS ziurtagiria) Cloudflare-k kudeatutako domeinuetarako sarbidea behar duten erronkak."

# libretranslate
msgid "The `Bash(*)` allow grants broad access to the `docker` CLI (alongside every other shell command) under the assumption that no production containers share the host. Non-mutating-image subcommands (`rm`, `kill`, `stop`, `system prune`, `volume rm`, `cp`) can disrupt or destroy container state. Under test-only usage, the blast radius is bounded to ephemeral state that can be recreated from the compose stack."
msgstr "The `Bash(*)` diru-laguntzak sarbide zabala ematea `docker` CLI (beste shell komandoekin batera) ekoizpen-edukiontziek ez dutela ostalaria partekatzen suposatuz. Irudiz aldatzen ez diren azpikomandoak (`rm`, `kill`, `stop`, `system prune`, `volume rm`, `cp`) edukiontzi-egoera eten edo suntsitu dezake. Probak bakarrik erabilita, leherketa-erradioa konposaketa-pilatik birsor daitekeen egoera iragankorrari lotuta dago."

# libretranslate
msgid "The `Bash(*)` allow lets the agent run any Makefile target without prompting. The `Makefile` is checked into git and reviewed on every pull request, so targets themselves are trusted. Every action a target performs still runs inside the sandbox."
msgstr "The `Bash(*)` agenteak edozein Makefile helburu exekutatzen uzten du, galdetu gabe. The `Makefile` git-a aktibatzen da eta tira-eskaera guztietan berrikusten da, beraz, helburuak beraiek fidagarriak dira. Helburu batek egiten duen ekintza orok harea-kutxaren barruan jarraitzen du."

# libretranslate
#, python-brace-format
msgid "The `Corefile.tmpl` MUST be the source of truth. It is rendered to `Corefile` by [coredns.py](../../cli/administration/deploy/development/coredns.py), which substitutes its `${VAR}` placeholders in-process, using values from `.env` (generated from [default.env](../../default.env), overridable through the CLI's environment)."
msgstr "The `Corefile.tmpl` Egiaren iturri izan behar du. Errendatzen da `Corefile` Egilea: [coredns.py](../../cli/administration/deploy/development/coredns.py), honek bere ordez `${VAR}` leku-markak prozesuan, balioak erabiliz `.env` (sortutakoa [default.env](../../default.env), CLIren ingurunetik oso urrun)."

# libretranslate
msgid "The `GitHub Actions self-hosted runner <https://docs.github.com/en/actions/hosting-your-own-runners/managing-self-hosted-runners/about-self-hosted-runners>`__ is an agent that runs GitHub Actions workflow jobs on your own infrastructure instead of GitHub-hosted machines."
msgstr "The `GitHub Actions self-hosted runner <https://docs.github.com/en/actions/hosting-your-own-runners/managing-self-hosted-runners/about-self-hosted-runners>`__ GitHub Actions-ek zure azpiegituretan lan egiten du, GitHub-en ordez."

# libretranslate
msgid "The `Makefile` is the human-facing command surface for the repo. It MUST expose stable targets that people and CI are meant to run directly."
msgstr "The `Makefile` Gizakiak zuzentzen duen aginte-azalera da. Helburu egonkorrak erakutsi behar ditu, jendeak eta CIk zuzenean exekutatzeko."

# libretranslate
msgid "The `OIDC` tree is a lazy group_var: it resolves in the consuming role's context, so the issuer family-aligns to that consumer (clearnet page → clearnet issuer, onion page → onion issuer). Inventory overrides therefore live under `OIDC_OVERRIDE:` — an inventory-level `OIDC:` block would shadow the lazy resolution and is rejected by a constructor assert."
msgstr "The `OIDC` zuhaitza alferra da group_var: kontsumo-funtzioaren testuinguruan erabakitzen du, eta, beraz, jaulkitzaile-familia kontsumitzaile horrekin bat dator (clearnet page → clearnet issuer, onion page → onion issuer). Inbentarioen gainjarriak bizi dira, beraz, `OIDC_OVERRIDE:` - inbentario maila bat `OIDC:` Blokeak ebazpen alferra itzalaraziko luke eta eraikitzaile batek ukatuko luke."

# libretranslate
msgid "The `Options` rule is what keeps a swarm host with NFS-backed volumes on the live copy (see [NFS-backed volumes](#nfs-backed-volumes)): such a volume is a separate filesystem, so a snapshot of the data root would capture it as an empty directory and the backup would succeed while holding nothing. The declaration is checked rather than the mount table, because docker mounts those volumes lazily and unmounts them when the last container stops."
msgstr "The `Options` araua da NFSren babeseko bolumenak dituen ostalari-multzo bat bizirik mantentzen duena (Ikusi [NFSren babeseko bolumenak](#nfs-backed-volumes)): horrelako bolumena fitxategi-sistema bereizia da, beraz, datuen erroaren argazki batek direktorio huts gisa hartuko luke eta babeskopiak ez luke ezer edukiko. Deklarazioa ez da muntatze-mahaia, docker-ek bolumenak lazily muntatzen dituelako eta azken edukiontzia gelditzen denean desmuntatzen dituelako."

# libretranslate
msgid "The `RUNNER_DISTRIBUTION` variable selects distro-specific package installation tasks (Debian, Ubuntu, Arch Linux, or Fedora/EL). The role is designed to be driven by the `make runner-ci-deploy` target; see the end-to-end guide below."
msgstr "The `RUNNER_DISTRIBUTION` aldagaiak paketeen instalazioko zereginak hautatzen ditu (Debian, Ubuntu, Arch Linux edo Fedora/EL). Eginkizuna gidatzen du `make runner-ci-deploy` helburua; ikus beheko amaierako gida."

# libretranslate
msgid "The ``(fqcn, version)`` pairs a requirements file declares, in order."
msgstr "The ``(fqcn, version)`` baldintza-fitxategi bat ezartzen du, ordenan."

