# libretranslate
msgid "What still blocks it is the transport. `server.py` speaks streamable HTTP upstream: `post_upstream` POSTs JSON-RPC to one URL and reads the reply, optionally SSE-framed. Baserow serves the older HTTP+SSE transport, where the client opens the stream and posts to the endpoint that stream announces — the shape `roles/test-e2e-cli/files/shared/mcp/contract.py` implements for `transport: sse` (\"the stream is the response channel and the endpoint it announces is the request channel\"). Fronting Baserow therefore needs that client transport in the adapter, or evidence that Baserow 2.3.3 also accepts a plain streamable-HTTP POST, which only a running instance can settle. A second consequence is waiting behind it: `web-app-n8n` speaks only `sse`, so it drops out of `allowed_consumers` the moment the surface becomes `streamable_http`."
msgstr "Mugitzen duena garraioa da. `server.py` HTTP korrontean gora doa: `post_upstream` POSTs JSON-RPC URL bati eta erantzuna irakurtzen du, aukeran SSE-markoa. Baserow-ek HTTP+SSE garraio zaharra zerbitzatzen du, non bezeroak korrontea irekitzen duen eta korronteak iragartzen duen amaierako puntura bidaltzen duen: forma `roles/test-e2e-cli/files/shared/mcp/contract.py` horretarako tresnak `transport: sse` (\"korrontea erantzun-kanala da eta adierazten duen puntua eskaera-kanala da\"). Baserow beraz, bezeroaren garraioa behar du moldagailuan, edo horren froga Baserow 2.3.3 HTTP POST sinple bat ere onartzen du, exekutatzen ari den instantzia bat bakarrik konpon dezakeena. Bigarren ondorio bat dago horren atzean: `web-app-n8n` bakarrik hitz egiten du `sse`, beraz, irten egiten da `allowed_consumers` azalera bihurtzen den unean `streamable_http`."

