# libretranslate
msgid "When a flow runs inside an iframe and login or OIDC clicks can reload it, the spec MUST treat the reload as a navigation event: await the next visible state or the new iframe URL, then reacquire the frame and rebuild locators before the next interaction. A stale iframe handle MUST NOT be reused across redirects."
msgstr "Iframe eta saio-hasierako edo OIDCren klikek birkargatzen dutenean, spec-ek birkarga nabigazio-gertaera gisa tratatu behar du: hurrengo egoera ikusgaiaren edo iframearen URL berriaren zain egon behar du, eta ondoren markoa birkokatu eta lokadoreak berreraiki hurrengo elkarrekintzaren aurretik. Iframe-aren helduleku zaharkitua ezin da birbideratzeetan berrerabili."

# libretranslate
msgid "When a host runs Docker Swarm with NFSv4-backed shared volumes (see [svc-storage-nfs-server](../svc-storage-nfs-server/) and [svc-storage-nfs-client](../svc-storage-nfs-client/)), this role **does not capture them** - provided some host is in the [svc-bkp-nfs-2-local](../svc-bkp-nfs-2-local/) inventory group. The lookup checks that group, not whether the role's last run actually succeeded, so a cluster whose export repository has never been deployed keeps that assumption unverified. The `backup_volume` lookup asks the same `swarm_nfs_backed()` predicate that drives the compose rewrite (`utils/storage/nfs.py`) and hands every export-backed volume to baudolo's `--volumes-no-backup-required`. Their single capture is then the export host's repository, which reads the same bytes from the server's own filesystem - no NFS round trip, no second copy racing the `link-dest` target."
msgstr "Ostalari batek korrika egiten duenean Docker Swarm NFSv-ekin4-Babestutako bolumen partekatuak (Ikusi [svc-storage-nfs-server](../svc-storage-nfs-server/) eta [svc-storage-nfs-client](../svc-storage-nfs-client/))rol hau **ez ditu harrapatzen** - ostalariren bat badago [svc-bkp-nfs-2-local](../svc-bkp-nfs-2-local/) inbentario taldea. Bilaketak talde hori egiaztatzen du, ez rolaren azken exekuzioak arrakasta izan duen ala ez, beraz, biltegia inoiz zabaldu ez den kluster batek suposizio hori egiaztatu gabe mantentzen du. The `backup_volume` Bilaketak gauza bera galdetzen du `swarm_nfs_backed()` Konposatua biridazten duen predikatua (`utils/storage/nfs.py`) esportatutako bolumen guztiak Baudolorenera eramaten ditu. `--volumes-no-backup-required`. Beren harrapaketa bakarra esportatzailearen biltegia da, zerbitzariko fitxategi-sistemako byte berdinak irakurtzen dituena - NFSko bidaia biribilik ez, bigarren kopiarik ez. `link-dest` Helburua."

# libretranslate
msgid "When a host runs Docker Swarm with NFSv4-backed shared volumes (see `svc-storage-nfs-server <../svc-storage-nfs-server/>`__ and `svc-storage-nfs-client <../svc-storage-nfs-client/>`__), this role **does not capture them** - provided some host is in the `svc-bkp-nfs-2-local <../svc-bkp-nfs-2-local/>`__ inventory group. The lookup checks that group, not whether the role’s last run actually succeeded, so a cluster whose export repository has never been deployed keeps that assumption unverified. The ``backup_volume`` lookup asks the same ``swarm_nfs_backed()`` predicate that drives the compose rewrite (``utils/storage/nfs.py``) and hands every export-backed volume to baudolo’s ``--volumes-no-backup-required``. Their single capture is then the export host’s repository, which reads the same bytes from the server’s own filesystem - no NFS round trip, no second copy racing the ``link-dest`` target."
msgstr "Ostalari batek korrika egiten duenean Docker Swarm NFSv-ekin4-Babestutako bolumen partekatuak (Ikusi `svc-storage-nfs-server <../svc-storage-nfs-server/>`__ eta `svc-storage-nfs-client <../svc-storage-nfs-client/>`__), rol hau **ez ditu harrapatzen** - ostalariren bat badago `svc-bkp-nfs-2-local <../svc-bkp-nfs-2-local/>`__ inbentario taldea. Bilaketak talde hori egiaztatzen du, ez rolaren azken exekuzioak arrakasta izan duen ala ez, beraz, biltegia inoiz zabaldu ez den klusterrak ez du hipotesi hori egiaztatu. The ``backup_volume`` Bilaketak gauza bera galdetzen du ``swarm_nfs_backed()`` Konposatua biridazten duen predikatua (``utils/storage/nfs.py``) esportatutako bolumen guztiak Baudolorenera eramaten ditu. ``--volumes-no-backup-required``. Beren harrapaketa bakarra esportatzailearen biltegia da, zerbitzariko fitxategi-sistemako byte berberak irakurtzen dituena - NFSko bidaia biribilik ez, bigarren kopiarik ez. ``link-dest`` Helburua."

# libretranslate
msgid "When a local deploy fails, you MUST validate the proposed fix inside a sidecar against the same image via `make compose-inner-run` (or `make compose-exec` against the live container) BEFORE starting another deploy, whenever the failure is reproducible there. The reproducible-there set includes: a container that crashes at startup, a misconfigured env var, an image-side bug, an in-container script that fails, or any failure whose root cause was traced to runtime state of the container. The only exception is failures that genuinely depend on multi-container or post-deploy state (network neighbours, persistent volumes, post-deploy Ansible hooks) — call that out explicitly in the iteration narrative."
msgstr "Lokalak huts egiten duenean, proposatutako finka balioztatu behar duzu irudi beraren aurkako albo-auto batean. `make compose-inner-run` (edo `make compose-exec` zuzeneko edukiontziaren aurka) Beste hedapena hasi aurretik, hutsegitea bertan behera uzten denean. Erreproduzigarri-multzoak barne hartzen ditu: hasieran huts egiten duen edukiontzi bat, gaizki konfiguratutako var bat, irudiaren aldeko bug bat, huts egiten duen script bat, edo edukiontziaren erro-kausa aurkitu den hutsegiteren bat. Salbuespen bakarra hutsegiteak dira, benetakoak multicontainer edo post-deploy egoeran. (sareko bizilagunak, bolumen iraunkorrak, gako ansibleak hedatzea) -esan hori iterazio-kontabilitatean."

