# libretranslate
#, python-brace-format
msgid "`\"sandbox\": { \"allowUnsandboxedCommands\": false }` removes the operator's ability to opt a single command out of the sandbox. The `dangerouslyDisableSandbox: true` parameter exposed by the Bash tool is rejected when this flag is `false`, so there is no per-call \"trust me, run this raw on the host\" path. Commands that legitimately cannot run inside the sandbox (e.g. operations requiring access to `~/.ssh` or `~/.gnupg`) MUST be invoked manually by the operator outside Claude Code rather than smuggled through an unsandboxed escape."
msgstr "`\"sandbox\": { \"allowUnsandboxedCommands\": false }` operadoreak aginte bakar bat hautatzeko duen gaitasuna kentzen du. The `dangerouslyDisableSandbox: true` Bash tresnak erakusten duen parametroa ez da onartzen bandera hau dagoenean `false`, beraz, ez dago deirik \"Fidatu nitaz, erabili gordin hau ostalarian\" Bide-izena. Legez bete ezin diren aginduak harea-ontzian (adibidez, sarbidea eskatzen duten eragiketak `~/.ssh` edo `~/.gnupg`) Claude Kodetik kanpoko operadoreak eskuz deitu behar du ihes egin beharrean."

# libretranslate
#, python-brace-format
msgid "`\"sandbox\": { \"autoAllowBashIfSandboxed\": true }` treats sandbox confinement as sufficient policy for Bash. It exists as defence-in-depth alongside the explicit `Bash(*)` allow entry in `permissions.allow`: with either in place, Bash commands run automatically as long as no `deny` or `ask` rule matches. The wildcard `Bash(*)` is the primary gate today; the flag guarantees the agent stays functional if that entry is ever narrowed or removed. This keeps the allowlist small (see [settings.md](settings.md)) and removes the friction of extending it for every new make target or script. The trade-off is that the sandbox MUST be correct: `allowWrite`, `denyRead`, and the network rules below are now the operative policy for what Bash can touch."
msgstr "`\"sandbox\": { \"autoAllowBashIfSandboxed\": true }` Sandbox-en konfinamendua Bash-entzako nahikoa politika gisa tratatzen du. Defentsa sakon gisa existitzen da, esplizituaren ondoan. `Bash(*)` sarrera baimendu `permissions.allow`: edozein lekutan, Bash komandoak automatikoki exekutatzen dira ez bada `deny` edo `ask` araua bat dator. Wildcard `Bash(*)` Ate nagusia da gaur; banderak agentearen funtzionamendua bermatzen du sarrera hori inoiz estu edo kentzen bada. Honek baimen-zerrenda txikia mantentzen du (Ikusi [settings.md](settings.md)) eta helburu edo script berri bakoitzarentzat hedatzeko marruskadura kentzen du. Salmenta da harea-kutxak zuzen egon behar duela: `allowWrite`, `denyRead`, Eta beheko sareko arauak dira Bashek uki dezakeenaren politika eragilea."

# libretranslate
#, python-brace-format
msgid "`$wgAIEditingAssistantActiveProviderConnection` is the JSON object `{url, endpoint, model, secret}` built from `MEDIAWIKI_LITELLM_CONNECTION`; `url` is `LITELLM_OPENAI_BASE_LOCAL_URL` and `secret` is this role's own `credentials.litellm_api_key`. The braces are mandatory: a brace-free value is re-wrapped as `{\"legacy\": ...}` upstream and the provider falls back to the vendor endpoint at `api.openai.com`."
msgstr "`$wgAIEditingAssistantActiveProviderConnection` JSON objektua da `{url, endpoint, model, secret}` Eraikia `MEDIAWIKI_LITELLM_CONNECTION`; `url` da `LITELLM_OPENAI_BASE_LOCAL_URL` eta `secret` rol honena da `credentials.litellm_api_key`. Giltzak derrigorrezkoak dira: giltzarik gabeko balioa berriro itzul daiteke. `{\"legacy\": ...}` upstream eta hornitzailea hornitzailearen amaierako puntura itzultzen da `api.openai.com`."

