# libretranslate
msgid "`FORCE_CANCEL_AFTER_SECONDS` turns the cancel into an escalation. A cancel request does not stop a running step: the runner asks it to end, and a step that ignores the signal keeps going until its own `timeout-minutes`, which is 350 for a deploy. The concurrency group holds the newer run on `pending` until the occupant is *terminal*, not until it is cancel-requested, so a superseded sweep can block its branch for hours after being told to stop -- measured at eight minutes and counting, with ten deploy jobs untouched. After the wait, every run that is still not `completed` gets [`force-cancel`](https://docs.github.com/en/rest/actions/workflow-runs), which bypasses the conditions that keep it alive. The skipped cleanup steps are the price, and for a run that has already been superseded its artefacts are of no use to anyone. Leave the variable unset to cancel and walk away, which is what a closed pull request and a deleted branch want."
msgstr "`FORCE_CANCEL_AFTER_SECONDS` bertan behera uztea eskalatze bat da. Ezeztatze-eskaerak ez du geldialdirik egiten: korrikalariak amaitzeko eskatzen dio, eta seinaleari ezikusi egiten dion urrats batek bere kabuz jarraitzen du. `timeout-minutes`, hau da: 350 zabaltzeko. Konkurrentzi taldeak lasterketa berria du `pending` Okupatzailea iritsi arte *terminala*Ez, bertan behera uztea eskatu arte, beraz, ordezko garbiketa batek bere adarra blokeatu dezake, gelditzeko esan ondoren, zortzi minututan neurtua eta zenbatua, hamar deplegaziorik gabe. Itxaron ondoren, oraindik ez dagoen lasterkaldi bakoitza `completed` lortu [`force-cancel`](https://docs.github.com/en/rest/actions/workflow-runs), Bizirik mantentzen duten baldintzak gainditzen dituena. Garbiketa-urrats saltatuak prezioa dira, eta bere artefaktuak gainditu dituen exekuzioak ez du ezertarako balio. Utzi aldagaia bertan behera uztea eta alde egitea, hori da eskaera itxi bat eta ezabatutako adar bat."

