msgid "`Test E2E Cli <https://example.com/>`__ is an application."
msgstr "`Test E2E Cli <https://example.com/>`__ Aplikazio bat da."

# libretranslate
msgid "`ToolServerConnection.auth_type: system_oauth` resolves the caller's token through `oauth_manager.get_oauth_token(user.id, oauth_session_id)` and presents it as the Bearer"
msgstr "`ToolServerConnection.auth_type: system_oauth` Deitzailearen tokena ebazten du `oauth_manager.get_oauth_token(user.id, oauth_session_id)` eta hartza bezala aurkezten du."

# libretranslate
msgid "`Unit tests` verify isolated logic."
msgstr "`Unit tests` logika isolatua egiaztatu."

# libretranslate
msgid "`UsersLookup` yields the `no-reply` user dict used to derive `from` and `password`. Missing entries MUST yield an empty dict. The fallback for `from` is then `root@<inventory_hostname>.localdomain`."
msgstr "`UsersLookup` amore ematen du `no-reply` erabiltzailearen diktak lortzeko erabiliak `from` eta `password`. Sarrera faltak diktaketa huts bat eman behar du. Atzerapena: `from` orduan `root@<inventory_hostname>.localdomain`."

# libretranslate
msgid "`Visual Studio Code <https://code.visualstudio.com/>`__ is a powerful source code editor with a wide plugin ecosystem, supporting development workflows across many languages and platforms. See also the `Arch Wiki - Development Tools <https://wiki.archlinux.org/title/Category:Development>`__ and general `Software Engineering <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Software_engineering>`__ on Wikipedia."
msgstr "`Visual Studio Code <https://code.visualstudio.com/>`__ Iturburu-kodeen editore ahaltsua da, pluginen ekosistema zabala duena, hizkuntza eta plataforma askotan garapen-fluxuak onartzen dituena. Ikus, gainera `Arch Wiki - Development Tools <https://wiki.archlinux.org/title/Category:Development>`__ eta orokorra `Software Engineering <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Software_engineering>`__ Wikipedian."

msgid "`Visual Studio Code <https://github.com/microsoft/vscode>`__ in a selectable flavor: the distribution’s Code - OSS build, VSCodium, or Microsoft’s own binary."
msgstr ""

# libretranslate
msgid "`WordPress <https://en.wordpress.org/>`__ is a versatile and widely used `content management system (CMS) <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Content_management_system>`__ that powers millions of websites, from blogs and portfolios to e-commerce and corporate sites. This deployment provides a containerized WordPress instance optimized for multisite operation, advanced media management, and extensive plugin support, allowing you to fully leverage the rich features of the WordPress software."
msgstr "`WordPress <https://en.wordpress.org/>`__ moldakorra eta oso erabilia da `content management system (CMS) <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Content_management_system>`__ Milioika webgune, blog eta zorrotik merkataritza elektronikora eta gune korporatiboetara. Hedapen honek edukiontzi bat eskaintzen du WordPress adibidez, multisite eragiketarako optimizatua, multimedia-kudeaketa aurreratua eta pluginen euskarri zabala, eta aukera ematen dizu funtzionalitate aberatsak erabat aprobetxatzeko. WordPress softwarea."

# libretranslate
msgid "`Zammad <https://zammad.org/>`__ is an open-source helpdesk and ticketing system. Agents handle customer requests across email, chat, phone and web; customers can open tickets from a self-service portal."
msgstr "`Zammad <https://zammad.org/>`__ kode irekiko laguntza-sistema da. Agenteek bezeroen eskaerak posta elektronikoz, berriketaz, telefonoz eta web bidez kudeatzen dituzte; bezeroek autozerbitzuko atari batetik sarrerak ireki ditzakete."

# libretranslate
msgid "`Zoom <https://zoom.us/>`__ is a popular video conferencing application for online meetings, webinars, and collaboration."
msgstr "`Zoom <https://zoom.us/>`__ Bideokonferentzia aplikazio ezaguna da lineako bileren, webinarren eta lankidetzaren artean."

# libretranslate
msgid "`[user@]host:/dev/...` → a device on the host, recovered over ssh then pulled; `[user@]host:/image` → the image is pulled and recovered locally (`device` / `full`)"
msgstr "`[user@]host:/dev/...` → ostalarian zegoen gailu bat, ssh-aren gainetik berreskuratua, gero tiraka; `[user@]host:/image` → Irudia lokalki atera eta berreskuratzen da (`device` / `full`)"

# libretranslate
msgid "`_as_bool` MUST accept the usual string forms (`true|false|yes|no|1|0|on|off`), booleans, and numbers. Every boolean decision in the fallbacks MUST use it so that `SYSTEM_EMAIL_*` values coming from YAML, environment variables, or already-coerced facts all behave the same."
msgstr "`_as_bool` Ohiko kate-formak onartu behar dira (`true|false|yes|no|1|0|on|off`), boolearrak eta zenbakiak. Atzerapeneko erabaki boolear guztiek erabili behar dute, beraz, `SYSTEM_EMAIL_*` YAMLtik datozen balioek, ingurune-aldagaiek edo dagoeneko egiaztatutako egitateek berdin jokatzen dute."

# libretranslate
msgid "`_compute` MUST delegate to three other lookup plugins rather than re-reading project state directly:"
msgstr "`_compute` Beste hiru bilaketa-plugin aurkeztu behar dira proiektua zuzenean irakurri ordez:"

# libretranslate
msgid "`_shared.js` — env + login helpers (`penpotOidcLogin`, `penpotLdapLogin`, `penpotNativeLogin`, `penpotRegister`)."
msgstr "`_shared.js` - env + saio-hasierako laguntzaileak (`penpotOidcLogin`, `penpotLdapLogin`, `penpotNativeLogin`, `penpotRegister`)."

# libretranslate
msgid "``\"line-above\"``: marker must be on the immediately preceding non-empty line. Blank lines between marker and construct break the association."
msgstr "``\"line-above\"``: markatzailea hutsik ez dagoen aurreko lerroan egon behar du. Marra hutsak markatzailearen artean eta elkarketa hautsi."

# libretranslate
msgid "``\"same-line\"``: marker must be on the construct's line."
msgstr "``\"same-line\"``: eraikitzailearen lerroan egon behar du markatzaileak."

