msgid "``Mastodon`` must survive translation, ``Cleanup Disc Space`` must not. Neither the capital nor a dictionary separates them: a brand is deliberately built from an ordinary word, so ``Mastodon``, ``Matrix``, ``Cursor`` and ``Shell`` all sit in an English dictionary, while a descriptive title regularly carries a term no dictionary holds. Measured against en_US-large, that rule would have released Mastodon, PostgreSQL and WordPress for translation and protected ``Automated Email Alerts for Service Failures``."
msgstr ""

# libretranslate
#, python-brace-format
msgid "``None`` empties the topic and is normalised to ``{}``: the closure resolver skips a non-mapping payload, so leaving the bare ``None`` would silently keep the services it was meant to drop."
msgstr "``None`` gaia husten du eta normalizatzen da ``{}``: itxitura-epaileak ez du ordaintzen, beraz, hutsa utzi du ``None`` isil-isilik gordetzen zituen bertan behera utzi behar ziren zerbitzuak."

# libretranslate
msgid "``None`` means the caller has to address the upstream registry: the image name is malformed, the mirror prefix is not configured, or neither the GitHub environment nor the git remote names the GHCR namespace."
msgstr "``None`` Horrek esan nahi du dei-egileak korronte-erregistroa zuzendu behar duela: irudiaren izena gaizki osatuta dago, ispiluaren aurrizkia ez dago konfiguratuta, ezta GitHub ingurunea ere, ezta GHCRren izen-lekua ere."

# libretranslate
msgid "``None`` on any indeterminate outcome (see :func:`fetch_manifest`), on an index without a matching platform, and on a manifest that carries no layers."
msgstr "``None`` edozein emaitza zehaztugabetan (Ikusi :func:`fetch_manifest`), bat datorren plataformarik gabeko indizean eta geruzarik ez duen adierazpenean."

# libretranslate
msgid "``None`` on any indeterminate outcome: unresolvable name, network error, auth wall, rate limit, non-200 status, or unparsable body."
msgstr "``None`` edozein emaitza zehaztugabetan: izen konponezina, sareko errorea, hegoaldeko horma, tasa-muga, ez...200 egoera, edo gorputz banaezina."

# libretranslate
msgid "``None`` when the title carries no deploy row. ``name`` is the display name, returned unresolved -- callers decode it through ``utils.roles.display``, which is what knows the role tree. ``tor``, ``distro`` and ``filesystem`` matter because a priority role runs the same mode and variant several times over, and only the glyphs tell those jobs apart -- a retrigger built from the title alone would otherwise replay a different combination than the one that failed."
msgstr "``None`` Tituluak ez duenean ilararik. ``name`` pantailaren izena da, ebatzi gabe itzuli da. Deitzaileek deskodetzen dute. ``utils.roles.display``, Hori da rol-zuhaitza ezagutzen duena. ``tor``, ``distro`` eta ``filesystem`` Lehentasunezko rol batek behin baino gehiagotan egiten du aurrera, eta glifek bakarrik esaten dituzte lan horiek."

# libretranslate
msgid "``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true`` is declared because the shared helper cannot reach Shopware’s logout, not because the journey is untestable. The only logout control lives in ``.sw-admin-menu__user-actions``, which the administration stylesheet keeps at ``display: none`` until its toggle is clicked, and that toggle is a bare ``div`` carrying no role, no ``aria-haspopup`` and no dropdown class — nothing in the helper’s trigger set matches it. Its second fallback, following a same-origin settings link, misses as well because the administration is hash-routed and every settings target is ``#/sw/settings/...``."
msgstr "``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true`` adierazten da laguntza partekatua ezin delako iritsi ShopwareBidaia ez da probaezina delako. Irteteko kontrol bakarra bizi da ``.sw-admin-menu__user-actions``, administrazioaren estilo-orriak mantentzen duena ``display: none`` txandakatzen den arte, eta txandakatze hori hutsa da. ``div`` paperik gabe, ez ``aria-haspopup`` Eta ez dago atzera-beherako klaserik, ez dator bat laguntzailearen abiarazlearekin. Bere bigarren atzerakadak, tonu bereko ezarpen-esteka baten ondoren, huts egiten du, baita administrazioa hash-routed delako eta ezarpen guztien helburua ere. ``#/sw/settings/...``."

# libretranslate
msgid "``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true`` is declared for a second, independent reason, and two separate obstacles justify it."
msgstr "``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true`` Bigarren arrazoi independentetzat jotzen da, eta bi oztopo ezberdinek justifikatzen dute."

# libretranslate
msgid "``PERSON_RE``     a multi-word proper name whose parts carry no dot. The"
msgstr "``PERSON_RE`` hitz anitzeko izen bat, zeinaren zatiek punturik ez duten. The"

