# libretranslate
msgid "``adapter``:         immutable source contract of a repository-owned adapter. ``category_allowlist`` suits an upstream that switches whole categories and offers no per-tool filter, where a tool allowlist would be unenforceable; ``mcp_passthrough`` fronts an upstream that already speaks MCP instead of translating REST. ``upstream_path`` names that upstream where it lives on the application's own vhost, so the proxy can hide it: reaching it directly walks past the allowlist the adapter exists to enforce. A provider whose upstream is a separate sidecar declares ``upstream_network`` instead and has nothing to hide there."
msgstr "``adapter``- Biltegi baten jabe den moldagailu baten iturburu-kontratu aldaezina. ``category_allowlist`` kategoria guztiak aldatzen dituen korrontera doa, eta ez du inolako iragazkirik eskaintzen, non tresna-baimenaren zerrenda ez den betegarria izango; ``mcp_passthrough`` REST itzuli ordez MCP hitz egiten duen korronte baten aurrean dago. ``upstream_path`` Aplikazioaren vhost-ean bizi den korrontean gora doazen izenak, proxy-ak ezkutatu ahal izateko: egokitzailearen baimen-zerrendatik zuzenean igarotzen da. Hornitzaile bat, zeina goi-korrontea beste albo-auto batek adierazten duen. ``upstream_network`` Horren ordez, ez dago ezer ezkutatzeko."

# libretranslate
msgid "``aliases``: list of DNS aliases. Default: ``[entity_name]`` for shared_net, ``[]`` for default_net"
msgstr "``aliases``: DNS aliasen zerrenda. Lehenetsia: ``[entity_name]`` zeren shared_net, ``[]`` zeren default_net"

# libretranslate
msgid "``allowed`` (default ``True``): the file (or dotted-path entry) MAY be present for a role of this type. Set ``allowed: False`` to forbid the file/entry on roles of this type so the lint layer can surface the offence with a precise reason."
msgstr "``allowed`` (lehenetsia ``True``): fitxategia (edo puntuzko bidearen sarrera) Horrelako paper bat izan daiteke. Ezarri ``allowed: False`` fitxategi/sarrera mota honetako roletan debekatzea, lint geruzak delitu hori arrazoi zehatz batekin azal dezan."

# libretranslate
msgid "``ansible_facts`` only carries ``docker0`` once the daemon has run, and the daemon config is written before that on a fresh node - facts are gathered at play start, and nothing re-gathers them after the install. Reading the fact alone therefore yields nothing on the very run that has to emit the address, which leaves the inner containers pointed at the clearnet resolver and the DinD DNS check failing on a domain only the node dnsmasq knows."
msgstr "``ansible_facts`` soilik ``docker0`` daemon-a exekutatu ondoren, eta daemon-aren konfigurazioa nodo berri batean idatzita dagoenean, gertaerak hasieran biltzen dira, eta ezerk ez ditu berriro biltzen instalazioaren ondoren. Beraz, kontua irakurtzeak ez du ezer ematen helbide bat igortzeko duen exekuzioan, eta horrek barneko edukiontziak argi-garbitzaileari eta DinD DNS egiaztapenak domeinu batean huts egiten dute dnsmasq nodoak bakarrik daki."

# libretranslate
msgid "``ansible`` (default)"
msgstr "``ansible`` (lehenetsia)"

# libretranslate
msgid "``ansible`` (default) wraps `matrix-docker-ansible-deploy <https://github.com/spantaleev/matrix-docker-ansible-deploy>`__ (MDAD). MDAD runs ~70 upstream sub-roles to deliver Synapse, Element, every supported bridge, Element Call, and Jitsi. Infinito.Nexus pins MDAD by commit, renders an MDAD inventory from ``services.matrix.*`` knobs, and disables MDAD’s bundled Traefik / Postgres / Redis so the central Infinito services back the stack."
msgstr "``ansible`` (lehenetsia) itzulbiratu `matrix-docker-ansible-deploy <https://github.com/spantaleev/matrix-docker-ansible-deploy>`__ (MDAD)MDAD exekutatzen da ~70 Goiko errekak Synapse, Element, onartutako zubi guztiak, Element Call eta Jitsi entregatzeko. Infinito.Nexus MDAD egikaritzearen arabera, MDADen inbentarioa egiten du ``services.matrix.*`` knobs, eta MDADen Traefik / Postgres / pakete sorta desgaitzen du Redis Beraz, Infinito zentralak pila berreskuratu zuen."

# libretranslate
msgid "``api.seaweedfs.s3.*`` is the public S3 endpoint and is reachable without SSO gating."
msgstr "``api.seaweedfs.s3.*`` Publikoa da S3 amaierako puntua eta iristekoa da SSO gating gabe."

# libretranslate
msgid "``application_id`` is read from the play variables unless given as ``application_id=``. ``key='expose'`` names the block instead of ``ports``, for Discourse's launcher file, whose ``expose:`` list is what becomes ``docker run -p`` there."
msgstr "``application_id`` erreproduzitzeko aldagaietatik irakurtzen da, ez bada ematen: ``application_id=``. ``key='expose'`` blokeari izena jarri ordez ``ports``, Zertarako? Discourseabiarazle-fitxategia, zeinaren ``expose:`` zerrenda da bihurtzen dena ``docker run -p`` Hortxe."

# libretranslate
msgid "``application_id`` of the client doing the discovery."
msgstr "``application_id`` bezeroaren aurkikuntza egiten."

# libretranslate
msgid "``auth_subject: administrator``: Home Assistant scopes the token to the account that minted it. This deployment mints it for the administrator, so a call arrives as the administrator whoever asked the client. Entity exposure still bounds the reach. Getting to the tool server is gated on the role’s ``mcp`` RBAC group."
msgstr "``auth_subject: administrator``-Etxeko laguntzaileak tokena ezartzen du. Hedapen honek administratzaileari eragiten dio, eta dei bat iristen da bezeroari galdetu zion administratzaileari. Entitatearen esposizioak oraindik irismena mugatzen du. Tresna-zerbitzarira iristea rolean dago. ``mcp`` RBAC taldea."

# libretranslate
msgid "``auth_subject: administrator``: Mattermost bounds a call by the account the token belongs to. This deployment mints that personal access token for the administrator account, so calls arrive with that account’s rights whoever asked. Reaching the tool server is gated on the role’s ``mcp`` RBAC group."
msgstr "``auth_subject: administrator``-Batez ere, tokenaren kontuko dei bat mugatzen du. Hedapen honek administratzailearen konturako sarbide pertsonalaren tokena metatzen du, beraz, deiak kontu horren eskubideekin iristen dira, nork eskatu. Tresna-zerbitzarira iristeak eragina du. ``mcp`` RBAC taldea."

# libretranslate
msgid "``auth_subject: administrator``: the API token is issued against the administrator account, so every call carries that account’s rights no matter who asked the client. Reaching the tool server is gated on the role’s ``mcp`` RBAC group, which is a separate grant from administering Jenkins."
msgstr "``auth_subject: administrator``: API tokena administratzaile-kontuaren aurka igortzen da, beraz, dei bakoitzak kontu horren eskubideak ditu, bezeroak galdetuta ere. Tresna-zerbitzarira iristeak eragina du. ``mcp`` RBAC taldea, administraziotik aparte ematen dena Jenkins."

# libretranslate
msgid "``auth_subject: administrator``: the personal access token is minted against the ``root`` account and stored under the ``administrator`` key, so every call carries that account’s rights no matter who asked the client. Reaching the tool server is gated on the role’s ``mcp`` RBAC group, which is a separate grant from administering GitLab."
msgstr "``auth_subject: administrator``: sarbide pertsonalaren tokena miazkatzen da ``root`` kontua eta gordea ``administrator`` Gakoa, beraz, dei bakoitzak kontu horren eskubideak ditu, bezeroak galdetutakoa edozein dela ere. Tresna-zerbitzarira iristeak eragina du. ``mcp`` RBAC taldea, administraziotik aparte ematen dena GitLab."

# libretranslate
msgid "``auth_subject: administrator``: the web-service token is issued against the administrator account, so a call carries that account’s rights regardless of who asked the client. The attached functions are read-only, which bounds what those rights can do here. Reaching the tool server is gated on the role’s ``mcp`` RBAC group."
msgstr "``auth_subject: administrator``: web-zerbitzuaren tokena administratzailearen kontutik bidaltzen da, beraz, dei batek kontu horren eskubideak ditu, bezeroari nork eskatu dion kontuan hartu gabe. Erantsitako funtzioak irakurtzeko soilik dira, eta horrek mugatzen du eskubide horiek zer egin dezaketen hemen. Tresna-zerbitzarira iristeak eragina du. ``mcp`` RBAC taldea."

# libretranslate
msgid "``auth_subject: service_account``. A call arrives at Baserow as the endpoint owner regardless of who asked the client, and reaches only the one workspace that account owns. That is the second bound under the adapter’s allowlist, not a substitute for it."
msgstr "``auth_subject: service_account``. Dei bat iristen da Baserow azken puntuaren jabea bezeroari galdetu ziona kontuan hartu gabe, eta kontua duen laneko area bakarra iristen da. Egokitzailearen baimen-zerrendako bigarren muga da, ez ordezkoa."

# libretranslate
msgid "``auth_subject: service_account``: ```tasks/utils/mcp/token.yml`` <./tasks/utils/mcp/token.yml>`__ creates the account ``NEXTCLOUD_MCP_USERNAME`` with ``occ user:add`` if it is missing, mints the app password against that account, and stores it under ``mcp.credential.owner``. Every call carries that account’s rights, not the administrator’s, no matter who asked the client. Reaching the tool server is gated on the role’s ``mcp`` RBAC group, which is a separate grant from holding a Nextcloud account."
msgstr "``auth_subject: service_account``: ```tasks/utils/mcp/token.yml`` <./tasks/utils/mcp/token.yml>`__ creates the account ``NEXTCLOUD_MCP_USERNAME`` with ``occ user:add`` if it is missing, mints the app password against that account, and stores it under ``mcp.credential.owner``. Every call carries that account’s rights, not the administrator’s, no matter who asked the client. Reaching the tool server is gated on the role’s ``mcp`` RBAC taldea, aparteko diru-laguntza da, eta Nextcloud kontua."

# libretranslate
msgid "``auth_subject``:    identity MCP calls execute as. ``user`` and ``oidc`` additionally require a ``delegation`` block, because a rendered deployment bearer is a service account no matter what the metadata claims."
msgstr "``auth_subject``: Identitatea MCP deiak exekutatu egiten dira. ``user`` eta ``oidc`` Gainera, beharrezkoa da ``delegation`` blokea, inplementazio-eramaile errendatua zerbitzu-kontua delako, metadatuek zer esaten duten kontuan hartu gabe."

# libretranslate
msgid "``auth_type: bearer`` with the token from the discovery data"
msgstr "``auth_type: bearer`` aurkikuntza-datuen tokenarekin"

# libretranslate
msgid "``auth``:            authentication scheme guarding the endpoint."
msgstr "``auth``-Autentifikatzeko eskema amaierako puntua zaintzen."

# libretranslate
msgid "``auto`` is advisory and never fails the unit — every refusal is logged to the journal as ``baudolo-snapshot: live copy, <reason>``, so check there if a host you expect to snapshot does not. A stated ``btrfs``/``zfs`` fails the unit instead, which is the point of stating it. Before every snapshot the launcher also removes the ``.baudolo-*`` leftovers a killed run leaves inside the data root."
msgstr "``auto`` Aholkua da eta ez du inoiz unitatean huts egiten; uko oro egunkarira konektatuta dago. ``baudolo-snapshot: live copy, <reason>``, Beraz, begiratu ea espero duzun ostalariren batek ez badu argazkiak ateratzea. Agerpena ``btrfs``/``zfs`` unitateak huts egiten du horren ordez, eta hori adieraztea da helburua. Pantaila-argazkia egin aurretik, abiarazleak ere kentzen du ``.baudolo-*`` hildako bat geratzen da datu-erroaren barruan."

# libretranslate
msgid "``backend``: ``cloud`` or ``chezmoi``"
msgstr "``backend``: ``cloud`` edo ``chezmoi``"

# libretranslate
msgid "``base_dir`` (string): base directory for CA files"
msgstr "``base_dir`` (katea): CA fitxategien oinarrizko direktorioa"

# libretranslate
msgid "``baudolo-restore --empty`` pre-cleans the schema in one psql session and replays the dump in the next, so a consumer that boots in between recreates the schema and the replay dies on its own ``CREATE TABLE``. Hence the refusal while a consumer is up."
msgstr "``baudolo-restore --empty`` eskema psql saio batean garbitu eta hurrengo egunean irauli egiten du, beraz, eskema birsortzen duen kontsumitzailea bere kabuz hiltzen da. ``CREATE TABLE``. Horregatik, uko egitea kontsumitzailea prest dagoen bitartean."

# libretranslate
msgid "``bench new-site`` uses the central MariaDB’s ``root`` to create the per-site DB on first deploy."
msgstr "``bench new-site`` erdikoa erabiltzen du MariaDBda ``root`` DB per-site-a sortzea lehen aldiz zabaltzean."

# libretranslate
msgid "``biber`` only ever exists inside EspoCRM through OIDC auto-provisioning (``ESPOCRM_CONFIG_OIDC_CREATE_USER=true``, ```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__); the role itself seeds only the administrator account. In the ``services.sso.enabled: false`` matrix variants that provisioning path is gone and no native ``biber`` user exists, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true``. The ``administrator`` and ``guest`` personas run in every variant."
msgstr "``biber`` barruan bakarrik existitzen da EspoCRM OIDC auto-provisioning bidez (``ESPOCRM_CONFIG_OIDC_CREATE_USER=true``, ```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__); the role itself seeds only the administrator account. In the ``services.sso.enabled: false`` matrix variants that provisioning path is gone and no native ``biber`` user exists, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true``. The ``administrator`` and ``guest`` Pertsonaiak aldaki guztietan ibiltzen dira."

# libretranslate
msgid "``bond`` states how tightly a role couples to the service it declares: ``>= 1`` keeps the partner on the same host, ``< 1`` lets it live on its own. The value sits on the consumer's side of the relation, so the pair is directed and the two directions of one pair need not agree."
msgstr "``bond`` adierazten du zein gogor jokatzen duten bikoteek zerbitzuan: ``>= 1`` bazkidea ostalari berean mantentzen du, ``< 1`` Bere kasa bizi dadila. Balioa kontsumitzailearen harremanaren alde dago; beraz, bikotea zuzentzen da eta bi norabideek ez dute bat etorri behar."

# libretranslate
msgid "``c.wiki.example.com`` → **parent** ``wiki.example.com`` (plus ``example.com`` apex)"
msgstr "``c.wiki.example.com`` → **gurasoa** ``wiki.example.com`` (plus ``example.com`` apex)"

# libretranslate
msgid "``ca_cert_host`` is where sys-ca-selfsigned provisions the root CA on the host. The container-side bind-mount targets live in the ``CA_TRUST`` group_vars SPOT (``inject_cert_container`` / ``inject_wrapper_container``) and reach the standalone runtime scripts as env vars and CLI arguments."
msgstr "``ca_cert_host`` non dagoen sys-ca-selfsigned ostalariaren erroko ZEa hornitzen du. Edukiontziaren aldeko loturen helburuak bizi dira ``CA_TRUST`` group_vars SPOT (``inject_cert_container`` / ``inject_wrapper_container``) vars eta CLI argumentuak bezala, exekuzio-denboraren script bakarretara iritsi."

# libretranslate
msgid "``central_mariadb_root_password``: The root password for the MariaDB server."
msgstr "``central_mariadb_root_password``: Erroko pasahitza MariaDB zerbitzaria."

# libretranslate
msgid "``cert_host`` (string): host path to Root CA certificate"
msgstr "``cert_host`` (katea): Root CA ziurtagiriaren bide-izena"

# libretranslate
msgid "``classification``:  what this role is in the MCP audit. Required."
msgstr "``classification``: Eginkizun hau MCPren ikuskaritzan dago. Beharrezkoa."

# libretranslate
msgid "``comments`` is the parsed per-key comment map from default.env (see :func:`utils.env.parser.parse_static_env_with_comments`). Dynamic keys carry their comments via each handler's ``COMMENT`` constant. ``custom.env`` overrides run last (see :func:`apply_custom_env`)."
msgstr "``comments`` komentatzeko mapa da default.env (Ikusi :func:`utils.env.parser.parse_static_env_with_comments`). Gako dinamikoek iruzkinak eramaten dituzte kudeatzaile bakoitzaren bidez ``COMMENT`` Etengabe. ``custom.env`` gainjarri azkena (Ikusi :func:`apply_custom_env`)."

# libretranslate
msgid "``compose build`` re-bakes the static output whenever the cloned content changes, so deploys are content-driven without any runtime build step."
msgstr "``compose build`` klonatutako edukia aldatzen den bakoitzean, irteera estatikoa berriro ezabatzen du, beraz, hedapenak edukiz bideratzen dira, exekuzio-denborarik eraiki gabe."

# libretranslate
msgid "``compose`` (deprecated)"
msgstr "``compose`` (Zaharkitua)"

# libretranslate
msgid "``compose`` is the in-repo Docker Compose stack. It remains installable but receives no new features."
msgstr "``compose`` da Docker Compose pila. Instalagarria izaten jarraitzen du, baina ez du ezaugarri berririk jasotzen."

# libretranslate
msgid "``compose`` or ``swarm`` to pin every image to that track, ``rotate`` to split the images across both."
msgstr "``compose`` edo ``swarm`` irudi bakoitza pista horretara eramateko, ``rotate`` irudiak bietan banatzea."

# libretranslate
msgid "``composer install`` failed."
msgstr "``composer install`` Huts egin du."

# libretranslate
msgid "``config.access_grants: []``, administrator-only rather than public"
msgstr "``config.access_grants: []``, administratzaileak bakarrik, publikoak baino."

# libretranslate
msgid "``consumer_not_allowed`` is a decision and simply narrows the result. ``transport_unsupported``, ``auth_unsupported``, ``endpoint_unreachable`` and ``tools_unenforceable`` mean the provider did authorize this consumer and the connection still cannot be rendered, so they abort the run instead of disappearing quietly: a client that silently ends up with fewer tools than the deployment declared is indistinguishable from one that works."
msgstr "``consumer_not_allowed`` erabakia da, eta emaitza murrizten du. ``transport_unsupported``, ``auth_unsupported``, ``endpoint_unreachable`` eta ``tools_unenforceable`` Hornitzaileak kontsumitzaile horri baimena eman zion eta konexioa oraindik ezin da errendatu, beraz, exekuzioa bertan behera utzi zuten lasai desagertu ordez: isil-isilik amaitzen den bezeroa lan egiten duenarengandik bereizi ezin daitekeen hedapena baino tresna gutxiagorekin amaitzen da."

# libretranslate
msgid "``consumer``: optional override"
msgstr "``consumer``: aukerako gainidazketa"

# libretranslate
msgid "``container system prune -a -f`` to remove unused Docker resources."
msgstr "``container system prune -a -f`` erabili gabeko Docker baliabideak kentzeko."

# libretranslate
msgid "``core`` for every language but the source language, ``docs`` for the languages LibreTranslate supports."
msgstr "``core`` hizkuntza bakoitzeko, iturburu-hizkuntza izan ezik, ``docs`` hizkuntzetarako LibreTranslate euskarriak."

# libretranslate
msgid "``credential_missing`` is the one authorized rejection that does not abort, because a provider deploying later in the same play has not written its secret yet. That exemption ends at the reconciliation stage, which runs once every provider has: ``assert_authorized_are_renderable(discovery, strict=True)`` treats it as fatal there."
msgstr "``credential_missing`` Amore ematen ez duen uko baimendua da, zeren eta gero joko berean hedatzen ari den hornitzaile batek ez du oraindik bere sekretua idatzi. Salbuespen hori adiskidetze-fasean amaitzen da, hornitzaile bakoitzak behin exekutatzen duena: ``assert_authorized_are_renderable(discovery, strict=True)`` Izugarria da."

# libretranslate
msgid "``credential``:      which principal the provider authenticates as, and where its secret is read from. Replaces the administrator token path."
msgstr "``credential``: hornitzailea identifikatzen duena eta bere sekretua nondik irakurtzen den. Administratzailearen bide-izena ordezten du."

# libretranslate
msgid "``credentials.mcp_bearer``, sent as ``Authorization: Bearer <bearer>``"
msgstr "``credentials.mcp_bearer``, bidalia ``Authorization: Bearer <bearer>``"

# libretranslate
msgid "``custom.env`` is the operator's untracked override file; its values win over static defaults AND handler-computed values."
msgstr "``custom.env`` operadorearen gainjarritako fitxategia da; balioek lehenetsi estatiko eta kudeatzaileen balioen gainetik irabazten dute."

# libretranslate
msgid "``database_name``: The name of the initial database to create."
msgstr "``database_name``: Sortu beharreko hasierako datu-basearen izena."

# libretranslate
msgid "``database_password``: The password for the database user."
msgstr "``database_password``: Datu-basearen erabiltzailearen pasahitza."

# libretranslate
msgid "``database_username``: The username for the database user."
msgstr "``database_username``: Datu-basearen erabiltzailearen erabiltzaile-izena."

# libretranslate
msgid "``days`` (int): certificate validity"
msgstr "``days`` (Int): ziurtagiriaren baliozkotasuna"

# libretranslate
msgid "``default-address-pools`` is where docker takes that address from, so the declaration answers before the daemon exists and answers identically afterwards. That also keeps daemon.json byte-identical across passes, which the fact-derived value could not: it appeared only from the second run on and restarted the container runtime under a live stack."
msgstr "``default-address-pools`` Dockerrek helbide hori hartzen duen lekua da, beraz, daemona existitu aurretik erantzuten du eta gero berdin erantzuten du. Horrek ere irauten du daemon.json Zeharkako pasabideak, egitateak eskatutako balioak ezin zituenak: bigarren irteeratik bakarrik agertu zen eta edukiontziaren exekuzio-denbora berrabiarazi zuen pila bizi baten azpian."

# libretranslate
msgid "``delegation``:      recorded proof, at one exact upstream version, that per-user token acquisition, refresh, audience binding and revocation exist."
msgstr "``delegation``: grabatutako froga, bertsio zehatz batean, erabiltzailearen tokena eskuratzeko, freskatzeko, ikusleen lotura eta errebokatzea existitzen direla."

# libretranslate
msgid "``deployment`` restricts to roles present anywhere in ``groups``, which is what a container-network consumer can actually reach; ``all`` returns every declaring role, deployed or not."
msgstr "``deployment`` edozein lekutan dauden roletara mugatzen du ``groups``, Hori da edukiontzi-sareko kontsumitzaile batek lor dezakeena; ``all`` funtzio deklaratzaile oro itzultzen du, hedatua edo ez."

# libretranslate
msgid "``dest``: destination path (required for ``cloud``)"
msgstr "``dest``: helburuko bidea (beharrezkoa ``cloud``)"

# libretranslate
msgid "``direction``:       whether the role exposes MCP, consumes it, or both."
msgstr "``direction``: Funtzioak MCP erakusten duen ala ez, kontsumitzen du, edo biak."

# libretranslate
msgid "``discourse``: the WP->Discourse post round-trip scenario. Disabling Discourse skips it; front-page reachability and CSP baselines stay active."
msgstr "``discourse``: WP->Discourse Post round-trip agertokia. Desitxuratzea Discourse saltatzen du; aurreko orrialdearen irisgarritasuna eta CSP oinarri-lerroak aktibo daude."

# libretranslate
msgid "``docker_name``    the explicit ``name:`` field (alias for ``name``"
msgstr "``docker_name`` esplizitua ``name:`` eremua (aliasa ``name``"

# libretranslate
msgid "``domains``: canonical and alias domains"
msgstr "``domains``: domeinu kanonikoak eta aliasak"

# libretranslate
msgid "``dotlinker_apply`` (default: ``true``): run ``doli pull`` after adding mappings"
msgstr "``dotlinker_apply`` (lehenetsia: ``true``): ``doli pull`` mapak gehitu ondoren"

# libretranslate
msgid "``dotlinker_cli_name`` (default: ``doli``)"
msgstr "``dotlinker_cli_name`` (lehenetsia: ``doli``)"

# libretranslate
msgid "``dotlinker_config_path`` (default: ``~/.config/dotlinker/config.yaml``)"
msgstr "``dotlinker_config_path`` (lehenetsia: ``~/.config/dotlinker/config.yaml``)"

# libretranslate
msgid "``dotlinker_package_name`` (default: ``doli``)"
msgstr "``dotlinker_package_name`` (lehenetsia: ``doli``)"

# libretranslate
msgid "``dotlinker_replace`` (default: ``true``): pass ``--replace`` to ``doli add``"
msgstr "``dotlinker_replace`` (lehenetsia: ``true``): ``--replace`` - ``doli add``"

# libretranslate
msgid "``dotlinker_user`` (required): user to run ``doli`` as"
msgstr "``dotlinker_user`` (beharrezkoa da): erabiltzailea exekutatzeko ``doli`` bezala"

msgid "``dsk-gnt-cursor`` and ``dsk-gnt-pi`` carry no entry in that map. Cursor is a full editor rather than an extension, and neither vendor publishes an extension on Open VSX, so there is nothing to install into Code for them. Both agents are used from their own binary."
msgstr ""

# libretranslate
msgid "``enabled`` (bool)"
msgstr "``enabled`` (boolearra)"

# libretranslate
msgid "``endpoint``:        connection metadata for clients (server roles only)."
msgstr "``endpoint``: konexio metadatuak bezeroentzat (zerbitzariaren rolak soilik)."

# libretranslate
msgid "``enforced`` onions every capable row, ``disabled`` none, ``exclusive`` drops the rows that cannot take one, ``auto`` rotates."
msgstr "``enforced`` lerro trebe guztiak, ``disabled`` bat ere ez. ``exclusive`` bat hartu ezin duten errenkadak erortzen dira, ``auto`` Biratu."

msgid "``entries_only=true`` returns those strings as a list instead of the rendered block, for a container that is not described by a compose file at all: ``web-app-discourse`` is built by discourse_docker's ``launcher``, whose only argument surface is ``docker_args:`` in its ``app.yml``, so it needs ``--add-host=<entry>`` lines."
msgstr ""

# libretranslate
msgid "``entries`` is a list of dotted-path facts about the file's content. Each entry carries the same ``mandatory`` and ``allowed`` semantics described above and adds a ``marker`` flag (default ``False``): ``marker: True`` declares the path as the type marker for the surrounding type entry. :func:`utils.roles.type.get_role_types` walks every ``marker: True`` entry; each marker that resolves to a non-empty value in the role's file adds the surrounding type to the role's type set. ``application_id`` for ``application`` and ``system_service_id`` for ``system-service`` are the canonical markers."
msgstr "``entries`` Fitxategiaren edukiari buruzko egitate puntutuen zerrenda da. Sarrera bakoitzak berdin darama. ``mandatory`` eta ``allowed`` goian azaldutako semantika bat gehitzen du ``marker`` bandera (lehenetsia ``False``): ``marker: True`` Bide-izena adierazten du inguruko sarrera motaren markatzaile gisa. :func:`utils.roles.type.get_role_types` ibilaldi bakoitza ``marker: True`` Sarrera; paperaren fitxategian hutsik ez dagoen balio bati aurre egiten dion markatzaile bakoitzak inguruko mota gehitzen dio. ``application_id`` zeren ``application`` eta ``system_service_id`` zeren ``system-service`` Markatzaile kanonikoak dira."

# libretranslate
msgid "``entry-manual-steer.yml`` declares a ``run-name:`` that interpolates the dispatch inputs. Once a run has started, that title is the only record of them: the REST API answers ``inputs: null`` for a workflow_dispatch run. Anything that wants to know what a run was dispatched with therefore parses the title — and parsing it against a hand-copied format would drift the moment the workflow changes, silently and without a failing test."
msgstr "``entry-manual-steer.yml`` a ``run-name:`` horrek bidalketa-sarrerak interpolatzen ditu. Behin korrika hasita, titulu hori da haien erregistro bakarra: API Erantzunak ``inputs: null`` a workflow_dispatch korrika. Exekutatzea zer den jakin nahi duen edozerk, beraz, izenburua aztertzen du, eta eskuz egindako formatu baten aurka aztertzen bada, lan-fluxua aldatzen den momentuan, isilean eta proba hutsik egin gabe."

# libretranslate
msgid "``ephemeral`` publishes the container port on a host port docker picks, for a service addressed only through the compose network."
msgstr "``ephemeral`` edukiontzi-portua argitaratzen du ostalari-portu batean, konposaketa-sarearen bidez bakarrik zuzendutako zerbitzu baterako."

# libretranslate
msgid "``exposed`` is an explicit per-service opt-in (default false) that makes the service reachable over the node onion: its port gets a dedicated ``HiddenServicePort``. Because ``applications`` is the variant-merged config (base ``meta/services.yml`` deep-merged with the round's ``meta/variants.yml`` override), a service is forwarded only in the variant/config where it sets ``exposed: true`` — which is exactly what lets the two DB variants be tested over Tor (v0 exposed -> reachable, v1 not -> refused)."
msgstr "``exposed`` zerbitzuko aukera esplizitua da (faltsua) eta horrek zerbitzua nodoaren tipularen gainean helgarri egiten du: bere ataka dedikatua da ``HiddenServicePort``. zeren eta ``applications`` aldagarriaren konfigurazioa da (oinarria ``meta/services.yml`` Giroan murgildurik. ``meta/variants.yml`` gainjarri), zerbitzua ezartzen duen aldaeraren/konfigurazioaren bidez bakarrik birbidaltzen da. ``exposed: true`` -Horixe da Torren gainean bi DB aldakiak probatzen uzten duena. (v0 agerian -> eskuragarria, v1 ez -> ukatuta)."

# libretranslate
msgid "``exposure``:        who may reach the endpoint."
msgstr "``exposure``: amaieraraino irits daitekeena."

# libretranslate
msgid "``extra_hosts=``, whatever the call site needs on top: a peer's overlay VIP, or a partner service reachable only on the host."
msgstr "``extra_hosts=``, Dei-guneak goian behar duen guztia: VIP gainjarri bat, edo ostalariak bakarrik eskura dezakeen zerbitzu bat."

# libretranslate
msgid "``false`` while MCP servers are discovered"
msgstr "``false`` MCP zerbitzariak aurkitu bitartean"

# libretranslate
msgid "``family`` is the ``os_family`` ansible reports for the host. Callers that have facts (the action plugin) pass it, so distributions outside the CI matrix - Manjaro, Mint, Rocky - still resolve through their family. Callers without facts (lints, the availability test) omit it and the family is derived from :data:`DISTRO_FAMILY`, which only covers the default matrix."
msgstr "``family`` da ``os_family`` ostalariaren txostenak. Gertaerak dituzten deitzaileak (Ekintzaren plugina) Pasa ezazu, beraz, CI matrizetik kanpoko banaketak - Manjaro, Mint, Rocky - oraindik ere familiatik igarotzen dira. Gertaerarik gabeko deiak (lintsak, erabilgarritasun-proba) alde batera utzi eta familia hortik dator :data:`DISTRO_FAMILY`, matrize lehenetsia soilik estaltzen duena."

# libretranslate
msgid "``filer.seaweedfs.s3.*`` serves the filer web UI behind an admin-only oauth2-proxy."
msgstr "``filer.seaweedfs.s3.*`` fitxategi-sarea eskaintzen du UI administratzaile baten atzean bakarrik oauth2-proxy."

# libretranslate
msgid "``files/configure-auth.sh`` (run on the deploy host) completes the first-run wizard (seeds the break-glass admin), installs both plugins via Jellyfin’s own ``/Packages`` installer, writes the plugin configs, and restarts."
msgstr "``files/configure-auth.sh`` (exekutatu ostalariaren gainean) lehen morroia osatzen du (hautsitako ispiluaren administratzailea hazi du)bi pluginak instalatzen ditu Jellyfinberea da ``/Packages`` instalatzailea, pluginaren konfigurazioa idazten du eta berrabiarazten du."

# libretranslate
msgid "``files/playwright.config.js``: shared Playwright configuration"
msgstr "``files/playwright.config.js``: partekatutako Playwright konfigurazioa"

# libretranslate
msgid "``files/python/policy.py`` validates it at startup. A contract missing a limit, carrying an empty allowlist, naming a wildcard path or lacking a pinned schema hash is refused before the process serves anything."
msgstr "``files/python/policy.py`` abioan balioztatzen du. Mugarik gabeko kontratua, baimen-zerrenda hutsa, bide-izen basatia edo eskema-hondorik ez duena, ukatu egiten da prozesuak ezertarako balio izan aurretik."

# libretranslate
msgid "``flags``: list of flags to AND. Default: ``[enabled, shared]``"
msgstr "``flags``: ETAren bandera zerrenda. Lehenetsia: ``[enabled, shared]``"

# libretranslate
msgid "``flavor`` picks the probe shape (see utils/docker/healthcheck/); each flavor brings its own interval, timeout, retries and start_period, and any of those may be overridden next to it. Without a ``flavor`` the entry must carry an explicit ``test`` argv. ``port_key`` selects another entry below ``ports.internal`` for services that expose their probe on a second port."
msgstr "``flavor`` zundaren forma hautatzen du (Ikusi utils/docker/healthcheck/); zapore bakoitzak bere tartea, denbora, erretriak eta start_period, Eta horietako edozein gainditu daiteke haren ondoan. gabe ``flavor`` Sarrerak esplizitua izan behar du ``test`` argv. ``port_key`` beheko beste sarrera bat hautatzen du ``ports.internal`` Bigarren portu batean kokatzen diren zerbitzuak."

# libretranslate
msgid "``force_regen`` (bool): if true, remove and regenerate key/cert"
msgstr "``force_regen`` (boolearra): egia bada, kendu eta birsortu gakoa/ziurtagiria"

# libretranslate
msgid "``forward[A]`` is the list of provider roles that ``A`` directly depends on (services it embeds). ``reverse[B]`` is the list of roles that directly depend on ``B`` (consumers that embed ``B``)."
msgstr "``forward[A]`` hornitzaileen rolen zerrenda da. ``A`` zuzenean araberakoa (kapsulatzen dituen zerbitzuak). ``reverse[B]`` rolen zerrenda da, zuzenean araberakoa. ``B`` (kapsulatzen duten kontsumitzaileak ``B``)."

# libretranslate
msgid "``getent`` honours nsswitch and cannot address a server, so on its own it cannot say which of the resolvers in resolv.conf refused. Where the distro ships a query tool, ask every nameserver directly; where it does not, the per-name verdicts still stand on their own."
msgstr "``getent`` ohoreak nswitch dira eta ezin du zerbitzari bati aurre egin, beraz, bere kabuz ezin du esan zein diren ebazpenak. resolv.conf Uko egin nion. Distroak kontsulta-tresna bat bidaltzen duenean, galdetu izen-zerbitzari guztiei zuzenean; non ez, izen-emateak beren kabuz daude oraindik."

# libretranslate
msgid "``group_vars/all/05_paths.yml`` is the single source of truth for host paths. The env layer (utils/env/handlers, exported by scripts/meta/env/load.sh) derives the ``INFINITO_*`` env keys from it; a set env wins so callers can override. When a tool runs outside that layer, e.g. a bare ``subprocess`` that does not inherit the env build, the value is read straight from the group_vars SPOT, so there is still no hardcoded literal default."
msgstr "``group_vars/all/05_paths.yml`` Egiaren iturri bakarra da bide ostalarientzat. Env geruza (utils/env/handlers, esportatuta scripts/meta/env/load.sh) hortik dator ``INFINITO_*`` env gakoak; env batek irabazi egiten du deitzaileek gainidazteko. Tresna bat geruza horretatik irteten denean, adibidez biluzi bat. ``subprocess`` horrek ez du env-a heredatzen, balioa zuzenean irakurtzen da. group_vars SPOT, beraz, ez dago lehenespen literalik."

# libretranslate
msgid "``host_alias=true``, which pins ``host.docker.internal`` at whatever reaches the host in the effective mode. A container that must talk to a service the host publishes -- msmtp relaying through the swarm ingress on :587, for instance -- needs the alias, and it must not hardcode ``host-gateway`` because that breaks under swarm for the reason below."
msgstr "``host_alias=true``, zein pin ``host.docker.internal`` ostalarira modu eraginkorrean iristen dena. Ostalariak zerbitzu batekin hitz egin behar duen edukiontzi batek argitaratzen du:587, adibidez, aliasa behar du, eta ez du hardcoderik behar. ``host-gateway`` zeren eta hori hor behean dagoen arrazoiagatik eten egiten baita."

# libretranslate
msgid "``http://giteamcpupstream:8080/mcp``, own network only"
msgstr "``http://giteamcpupstream:8080/mcp``, sare propioa soilik"

# libretranslate
msgid "``http://nginx:80/webservice/mcp/server.php`` on the shared MCP overlay"
msgstr "``http://nginx:80/webservice/mcp/server.php`` MCPren gainjartze partekatuan"

# libretranslate
msgid "``implementation``:  how the surface is provided, ordered by precedence."
msgstr "``implementation``: gainazala nola ematen den, lehentasunaren arabera ordenatua."

# libretranslate
msgid "``in_container`` exists because one template serves two consumers. The host's /root/.msmtprc is read by the host and loopback is right for it; the copy mounted at /etc/msmtprc is read inside a container, where 127.0.0.1 is that container's own loopback and nothing listens on it. Such a service must also emit ``lookup('container_extra_hosts')`` so the alias resolves."
msgstr "``in_container`` txantiloi batek bi kontsumitzaileri zerbitzatzen dielako existitzen da. Ostalariaren /root/.msmtprc-a ostalariak irakurtzen du, eta begizta zuzena da; /etc/msmtprc-en muntatutako kopia edukiontzi baten barruan irakurtzen da, non 127.0.0.1 edukiontziaren begizta bera da eta ez du ezer entzuten. Horrelako zerbitzuak ere igorri behar ditu. ``lookup('container_extra_hosts')`` Beraz, aliasak erabakitzen du."

# libretranslate
msgid "``indent=0`` collapses everything to the left edge - useful when the lookup is rendered into top-level YAML (no service wrapper)."
msgstr "``indent=0`` dena ezkerrera erortzen da, erabilgarria bilaketa maila goreneko YAML bihurtzen denean. (ez dago zerbitzu-itzultzailerik)."

# libretranslate
msgid "``ingress`` (default) emits the short ``\"host:published:container\"`` string; ``host`` emits the long block with ``mode: host``, which is what an edge role needs in swarm so the client address survives the hop."
msgstr "``ingress`` (lehenetsia) laburra igortzen du ``\"host:published:container\"`` katea; ``host`` bloke luzea igortzen du ``mode: host``, Hori da ertz-rol batek behar duena, bezeroaren helbideak aurrera egin dezan."

# libretranslate
msgid "``internal`` (default) reads ``ports.internal.<proto>``; ``same`` reuses the published port, for services that cannot remap (STUN/TURN, media relays)."
msgstr "``internal`` (lehenetsia) irakurri ``ports.internal.<proto>``; ``same`` Argitaratutako portua berrerabiltzen du, birmapa ezin dezaketen zerbitzuetarako (STUN/TURN, euskarri-erreleak)."

# libretranslate
msgid "``internal``, container network only"
msgstr "``internal``, edukiontzi-sarea soilik"

# libretranslate
msgid "``kas`` (Kubernetes agent server, workspaces), ``pages``, ``registry`` and ``mailroom`` are not deployed; ``gitlab.yml`` disables them."
msgstr "``kas`` (Kubernetes agente-zerbitzaria, laneko areak), ``pages``, ``registry`` eta ``mailroom`` Ez daude hedatuak; ``gitlab.yml`` desgaitzen ditu."

# libretranslate
msgid "``key_bits`` (int): RSA key size"
msgstr "``key_bits`` (Int): RSA gako-tamaina"

# libretranslate
msgid "``key_host`` (string): host path to Root CA private key"
msgstr "``key_host`` (katea): Root CA-ko gako pribaturako bide-izena"

# libretranslate
msgid "``key`` names the pinned key and defaults to ``version``; an entity with several pins declares a list of such blocks. The types are ``git_tags`` (repository), ``registry_tags`` (image), ``npm`` (package), ``http_regex`` (url, pattern) and ``script`` (path, run with the current version and printing the latest one)."
msgstr "``key`` izenpetutako tekla eta lehenetsiei ``version``; zenbait pin dituen entitate batek bloke horien zerrenda adierazten du. Motak dira ``git_tags`` (biltegia), ``registry_tags`` (irudia), ``npm`` (paketea), ``http_regex`` (url, eredua) eta ``script`` (Bide-izena, exekutatu uneko bertsioarekin eta inprimatu azkena)."

# libretranslate
msgid "``key``: services.<key>.* lookup base. Default: provides or entity_name"
msgstr "``key``: zerbitzuak.<key>.* Bilaketa-oinarria. Lehenetsia: eman edo entity_name"

# libretranslate
msgid "``kind``: ``services_flags`` (default) | ``database`` | ``mcp_client`` | ``web_facing`` | ``onion_sso``. ``mcp_client`` admits a role only when its ``mcp.direction`` is ``client`` or ``both`` AND it declares ``services.<own-entity>.mcp_consumer: true`` without the provider refusing it through ``mcp_consumer: false`` on that same entry, so a provider's network carries the clients it admitted rather than every client in the deployment. Being a client is not an admission: without the second condition one admission anywhere reaches every provider that opens its overlay."
msgstr "``kind``: ``services_flags`` (lehenetsia) -Bai. ``database`` -Bai. ``mcp_client`` -Bai. ``web_facing`` -Bai. ``onion_sso``. ``mcp_client`` rol bat onartzen du berea denean soilik ``mcp.direction`` da ``client`` edo ``both`` ETA adierazten du ``services.<own-entity>.mcp_consumer: true`` hornitzaileari uko egin gabe ``mcp_consumer: false`` sarrera horretan, hornitzaile baten sareak onartzen dituen bezeroak eramaten ditu, eta ez hedapeneko bezero guztiak. Bezero izatea ez da onarpen bat; bigarren baldintzarik gabe, sarrera bat hornitzaile guztietara iristen da."

# libretranslate
msgid "``last`` seeds the OCI pagination cursor: only tags sorting lexically after it are returned. Repos like GitLab CNG carry tens of thousands of commit-sha tags before the ``v*`` release tags, so an unseeded scan exhausts ``max_pages`` without ever reaching them."
msgstr "``last`` OCIren pizkundearen kurtsorea hazi zuen: itzuli ondoren, lexikoki ordenatutako etiketak bakarrik. Repos bezalakoak GitLab CNGk hamarnaka mila manu-formako etiketak eramaten ditu aurretik ``v*`` askatu etiketak, beraz, eskaneatzeko ihes ikusezin bat ``max_pages`` Inoiz iritsi gabe."

# libretranslate
msgid "``latest`` is the last commit of the default branch. It is built at start and rebuilt whenever a fetch finds a new commit; the previous build stays online until the new one replaces it."
msgstr "``latest`` adar lehenetsiaren azken ekintza da. Hasiera batean eraiki eta berreraiki egiten da erosketa batek beste bat aurkitzen duenean; aurreko eraikuntza linean egoten da, berriak ordeztu arte."

msgid "``laya``, ``torch`` or ``onnx``; the role refuses anything else"
msgstr ""

# libretranslate
msgid "``ldap``: the three RBAC scenarios additionally depend on LDAP group sync; disabling LDAP skips them alongside OIDC."
msgstr "``ldap``: hiru RBAC agertokiak LDAP taldearen sinkronizazioaren mende daude; LDAP desgaituz gero, OIDCrekin batera saltatzen ditu."

# libretranslate
msgid "``ldapauth`` is the only path that materialises a ``friendica.user`` row, so its enablement derives directly from the ``ldap`` service flag. The oauth2-proxy ``sso`` gate in front of the vhost is a front-door auth gate, not an addon bridge, and stays in ```meta/services.yml`` <./meta/services.yml>`__. The LDAP login path is covered by the existing LDAP Playwright spec (requirement 018), so no addon-specific spec is added."
msgstr "``ldapauth`` a gauzatzen duen bide bakarra da ``friendica.user`` errenkada, beraz, bere ezarpena zuzenean dator ``ldap`` Zerbitzuaren bandera. oauth2-proxy-a ``sso`` Ostalariaren aurreko atea atzeko ate bat da, ez zubi gehigarri bat, eta bertan geratzen da. ```meta/services.yml`` <./meta/services.yml>`... LDAPeko saio-hasieraren bide-izena lehendik dagoen LDAP Playwright espektroak estaltzen du (baldintza 018), Beraz, ez da gehigarri espezifikorik gehituko."

# libretranslate
msgid "``libaacs`` (AACS decryption library)"
msgstr "``libaacs`` (AACS desenkriptatze-liburutegia)"

# libretranslate
msgid "``libbluray`` (Blu-ray playback support library)"
msgstr "``libbluray`` (Blu-ray erreprodukzio euskarri-liburutegia)"

# libretranslate
msgid "``lifecycle``  — maturity marker filtered by ``cli meta roles lifecycle``."
msgstr "``lifecycle`` - Heldutasun-markatua iragazita ``cli meta roles lifecycle``."

# libretranslate
msgid "``limits``:          the request, response, timeout, concurrency, pagination and stream ceilings the surface enforces."
msgstr "``limits``: eskaera, erantzuna, denbora-muga, konkurrentzia, pginazioa eta korronte-sabaiak gainazalak betearazten ditu."

# libretranslate
msgid "``locale-gen`` only re-runs when the template changes"
msgstr "``locale-gen`` txantiloia aldatzean bakarrik exekutatzen da."

# libretranslate
msgid "``locale.conf``: sets ``LANG`` and ``LANGUAGE`` environment variables"
msgstr "``locale.conf``: multzoak ``LANG`` eta ``LANGUAGE`` inguruneko aldagaiak"

# libretranslate
msgid "``locale.gen``: uncomment or specify the locales you need"
msgstr "``locale.gen``: ez sartu edo zehaztu behar dituzun lokalak"

# libretranslate
msgid "``lookup('users', user_key).authorized_keys`` (list; may be empty)"
msgstr "``lookup('users', user_key).authorized_keys`` (zerrenda; hutsik egon daiteke)"

# libretranslate
msgid "``lookup('users', user_key).username`` (defaults to ``user_key``)"
msgstr "``lookup('users', user_key).username`` (lehenetsia ``user_key``)"

# libretranslate
#, python-brace-format
msgid "``lookup('volume', application_id)`` — return the WHOLE canonical registry as a dict keyed by semantic name. Useful for tasks that loop over every declared volume (e.g. NFS subdir pre-creation). Returns ``{}`` for roles with no meta/volumes.yml."
msgstr "``lookup('volume', application_id)`` - itzuli OMELEren erregistro kanonikoa izen semantikoak gidatutako dikta gisa. Baliagarria, deklaratutako bolumen guztiak begiztatzen dituzten zereginetarako (adibidez, NFS azpidir pre-sorkuntza)Itzultzen ``{}`` funtziorik gabe meta/volumes.yml."

# libretranslate
msgid "``lookup('volume', application_id, name)`` — return the normalised dict for a single semantic entry. The returned dict always carries:"
msgstr "``lookup('volume', application_id, name)`` -Itzul ezazu hiztegi normalizatua sarrera semantiko bakar baterako. Itzultzen den diktak beti darama:"

# libretranslate
msgid "``main.yml``: The main task file that handles the installation of GnuCash."
msgstr "``main.yml``: Instalazioa kudeatzen duen zeregin-fitxategi nagusia GnuCash."

# libretranslate
msgid "``main`` unless ``repo_root`` is a linked git worktree, whose branch is lowercased and every character outside ``[a-z0-9_-]`` replaced by ``-``; ``None`` when the worktree's git directory is not reachable, as inside a container that mounts only the checkout."
msgstr "``main`` ezean ``repo_root`` estekatutako lan-zuhaitza da, zeinaren adarra beheratua dagoen eta kanpoko karaktere guztiak ``[a-z0-9_-]`` ordeztua ``-``; ``None`` Lan-zuhaitzaren git direktorioa ezin denean eskuratu, faktura muntatzen duen edukiontzi baten barruan bezala."

# libretranslate
msgid "``make install-lint`` used to ask GitHub for each tool’s latest tag at install time. That made every installation depend on the network resolving ``api.github.com``, and it silently changed the linter version between two runs of the same commit. Pinning moves the version into the repository, where it is reviewable and reproducible."
msgstr "``make install-lint`` GitHub-i galdetu ohi zion tresna bakoitzaren azken etiketa instalatzeko orduan. Instalazio bakoitza sarearen arabera konpondu behar da. ``api.github.com``, eta isil-isilik aldatu zuen linterna-bertsioa, bi ilararen artean. Pinning-ek bertsioa biltegira eramaten du, non errebisagarria eta erreproduzigarria den."

# libretranslate
msgid "``make install`` completed on the control machine (installs Ansible and Python dependencies)."
msgstr "``make install`` Kontrol-makinan burutua (Ansible eta Python-en mendekotasunak instalatzea)."

# libretranslate
msgid "``mandatory`` (default ``False``): the file (or dotted-path entry) MUST be present and non-empty for a role of this type. Implies ``allowed: True``; setting ``mandatory: True`` together with ``allowed: False`` is a schema error."
msgstr "``mandatory`` (lehenetsia ``False``): fitxategia (edo puntuzko bidearen sarrera) Hemen egon behar du eta ez dago hutsik horrelako paper baterako. Inplikazioak ``allowed: True``; ezarpena ``mandatory: True`` elkarrekin ``allowed: False`` eskema-errorea da."

# libretranslate
msgid "``master.seaweedfs.s3.*`` serves the master web UI behind the same admin-only oauth2-proxy."
msgstr "``master.seaweedfs.s3.*`` UI maisuari eskaintzen dio administratzaile beraren atzean, oauth bakarra.2-proxy."

# libretranslate
msgid "``match`` keeps only the versions carrying that prefix, and ``strip`` removes it again, so a pin without the upstream's ``v`` stays without it."
msgstr "``match`` aurrizki hori duten bertsioak bakarrik gordetzen ditu, eta ``strip`` berriro kentzen du, beraz, pin bat igo gabe. ``v`` Geldi hor."

# libretranslate
msgid "``mcp-server`` pinned to ``0.190.ve5a_6581ffc96`` in ```files/plugins.txt`` <./files/plugins.txt>`__"
msgstr "``mcp-server`` pintatuta ``0.190.ve5a_6581ffc96`` barruan ```files/plugins.txt`` <./files/plugins.txt>`"

# libretranslate
msgid "``mcp.enabled`` resolves to ``true`` only when ``web-app-hermes``, ``web-app-openclaw`` or ``web-app-openwebui`` is part of the same deployment, and is ``false`` otherwise. While it is ``true`` the deploy:"
msgstr "``mcp.enabled`` Erabakiak: ``true`` bakarrik ``web-app-hermes``, ``web-app-openclaw`` edo ``web-app-openwebui`` hedapen beraren parte da, eta da ``false`` bestela. Dagoen bitartean ``true`` hedapena:"

# libretranslate
msgid "``mcp`` declares the Model Context Protocol surface GitLab serves natively from its Rails API."
msgstr "``mcp`` Testuinguru Modeloaren Protokoloaren azalera adierazten du GitLab bertako trenbideetatik zerbitzatzen du API."

# libretranslate
msgid "``meta/addons/`` is also the download list: ``MEDIAWIKI_EXT_NAMES`` keeps only the addons whose ``enabled`` resolves true, so a deployment without the matching service never pulls that tarball or runs composer for it."
msgstr "``meta/addons/`` deskargatzeko zerrenda ere bada: ``MEDIAWIKI_EXT_NAMES`` Gehigarriak bakarrik gordetzen ditu. ``enabled`` Egia erabakitzen du, beraz, bat datorren zerbitzurik gabe hedatzeak ez du inoiz kentzen tarbol hori edo konpositorea."

# libretranslate
msgid "``meta/categories.yml`` at the repository root declares the nested category tree every role name is derived from: the dash-joined path of a node is the role's category prefix (``web`` -> ``app`` yields ``web-app-*``), and nodes carry the ``invokable``, ``stage``, ``modes`` and ``run_after`` policy the dispatcher, the stage lookup and the inventory generator read."
msgstr "``meta/categories.yml`` biltegiaren erroan adierazten da kategoria-zuhaitz habiaratua rol-izen bakoitza nondik datorren: nodo baten bide-izena da kategoria-aurrizkia. (``web`` -> ``app`` amoreak ``web-app-*``), eta nodoek eramaten dute ``invokable``, ``stage``, ``modes`` eta ``run_after`` politika: bidalketa, eszena-bilaketa eta inbentario-sortzailea."

# libretranslate
msgid "``meta/categories.yml`` declares the ordered ``stages`` (constructor -> workstation -> server -> destructor, matching ``tasks/stages/0*.yml``) and a ``stage`` per top-level category. This module resolves a role to its stage and exposes the canonical stage order, so both the CLI (``cli.meta.roles.order``) and the ``stage_order`` / ``role_stage`` lookups read one source of truth."
msgstr "``meta/categories.yml`` Agindutakoa adierazten du ``stages`` (eraikitzailea -> lanpostua -> zerbitzaria -> suntsitzailea, bat datozenak ``tasks/stages/0*.yml``) a ``stage`` maila goreneko kategorian. Modulu honek bere agertokian rol bat ebazten du eta eszena-ordena kanonikoa erakusten du, beraz, biak CLI (``cli.meta.roles.order``) eta ``stage_order`` / ``role_stage`` Bilaketak egiaren iturri bat irakurtzen dute."

# libretranslate
msgid "``meta/distros.yml`` declares every distribution the project builds, tests and deploys on: the id used as ``INFINITO_DISTRO``, the ``os_family`` ansible reports for it, the Galaxy platform name, the upstream base image the development-environment matrix boots it from, and the templates the pkgmgr base image and the environment image references are rendered from."
msgstr "``meta/distros.yml`` Proiektuak eraikitzen, probatzen eta hedatzen dituen banaketa guztiak adierazten ditu: ``INFINITO_DISTRO``, ``os_family`` horrentzat txosten ansibleak, Galaxiako plataformaren izena, oinarrizko irudia, garapen-inguruneko matrizeak bota egiten du, eta txantiloiak pkgmgr oinarrizko irudia eta inguruneko irudiaren erreferentziak itzultzen dira."

# libretranslate
msgid "``meta/variants.yml`` defines three variants (mirrors the ``web-app-kix`` / ``web-app-zammad`` pattern):"
msgstr "``meta/variants.yml`` hiru aldaera definitzen ditu (ispiluak ``web-app-kix`` / ``web-app-zammad`` eredua):"

# libretranslate
msgid "``mode`` selects placement semantics:"
msgstr "``mode`` Jarduteko semantika hautatzen du:"

# libretranslate
msgid "``modes`` in ``meta/services.yml`` states where a role RUNS; ``skip`` in ``meta/tests.yml`` deactivates TESTING a mode without touching that capability."
msgstr "``modes`` barruan ``meta/services.yml`` Rol bat RUNS-en arabera; ``skip`` barruan ``meta/tests.yml`` Modu bat desaktibatzen du gaitasun hori ukitu gabe."

# libretranslate
msgid "``modes``: list of DEPLOYMENT_MODE values where this overlay applies"
msgstr "``modes``: zerrenda DEPLOYMENT_MODE gainjartzea aplikatzen den balioak"

# libretranslate
msgid "``mounts``         the raw mounts list, ``[]`` if absent"
msgstr "``mounts`` mendi gordinen zerrenda, ``[]`` baldin badago"

# libretranslate
msgid "``msgctxt`` prefixes of the messages to include, e.g. ``role:``."
msgstr "``msgctxt`` Mezuen aurrizkiak, adibidez. ``role:``."

# libretranslate
msgid "``mutating_proofs``: required once ``tools.mutating_tools_enabled`` is true. Names the artifact proving each of confirmation, authorization, idempotency, audit and reversal for the mutating variant, separately from the read-only one."
msgstr "``mutating_proofs``: Behin beharrezkoa ``tools.mutating_tools_enabled`` Egia da. Berrespena, baimena, idempotenzia, ikuskaritza eta aldagarritasuna frogatzen duen artefaktua izendatzen du, irakurritako bakarraz aparte."

# libretranslate
msgid "``name``           the EFFECTIVE docker volume name"
msgstr "``name`` EFFECTIVE bolumenaren izena"

# libretranslate
msgid "``name``: unique mapping id"
msgstr "``name``: mapatzeko ID bakarra"

# libretranslate
msgid "``networks.internet.dns`` arrives through ``-e @inventories/...`` and is read straight out of ``variables``, which hands back whatever the file contains. While that was a literal address nobody noticed; an expression there reached the daemon as its own source text and docker refused the config with ``ParseAddr(\"{{ ... }}\")``."
msgstr "``networks.internet.dns`` iristen ``-e @inventories/...`` eta zuzen irakurtzen da ``variables``, Fitxategiak daukan guztia atzeratzen duena. Helbide literala zen bitartean, ez zen inor ohartu. Adierazpen bat iritsi zen daemon-era bere iturburuko testu gisa eta docker-ek konfigurazioari uko egin zion. ``ParseAddr(\"{{ ... }}\")``."

# libretranslate
msgid "``new_text_or_None`` is ``None`` when nothing changed."
msgstr "``new_text_or_None`` da ``None`` ezer aldatu ez zenean."

# libretranslate
msgid "``nfs``            NFS opt-in (bool or dict), ``None`` if absent"
msgstr "``nfs`` NFS opt-in (boolearra edo diktua), ``None`` baldin badago"

# libretranslate
msgid "``noqa`` and ``nocheck`` are accepted as synonyms (case-insensitive) by this parser. By repo convention every project rule from ``docs/contributing/actions/testing/suppression.md`` MUST use ``nocheck:`` because ``# noqa: <code>`` is also parsed by ruff as a flake8 directive and triggers ``invalid-noqa-code`` warnings on every project-specific rule key. ``noqa:`` is reserved for real flake8 / ruff codes (``E402``, ``F401``, …). The ``direct-yaml`` lint enforces the convention by hard-rejecting the ``noqa:`` form."
msgstr "``noqa`` eta ``nocheck`` Sinonimo gisa onartzen dira (maiuskulak eta minuskulak bereizi gabe) analizatzaile honen bidez. Konbentzioaren arabera, proiektu bakoitzak bere arauak ``docs/contributing/actions/testing/suppression.md`` Erabili beharra dago ``nocheck:`` zeren ``# noqa: <code>`` ruff-ek ere aztertzen du flake gisa8 direktiba eta abiarazleak ``invalid-noqa-code`` Proiektu bakoitzaren arau-gako bakoitzaren abisuak. ``noqa:`` benetako flakearentzat gordeta dago8 /ruff kodeak (``E402``, ``F401``,...). The ``direct-yaml`` lintek konbentzioa behartzen du gogor baztertuz ``noqa:`` forma."

# libretranslate
msgid "``offset`` moves that start deliberately: it is how an operator reaches the tail without waiting for anything. It defaults to 0, so every run that does not ask for it deploys the same head and can be compared against the last one. This used to be derived from the sweep number instead, which bought tail coverage at the price of the head -- chunk 0 began wherever the arithmetic pointed, the rows that matter most ran only every few sweeps, and no two runs were comparable."
msgstr "``offset`` nahita hasten diren mugimenduak: eragile bat buztanera iristen da ezeren zain egon gabe. Lehenetsi egiten da 0, Beraz, eskatzen ez duen run bakoitzak buru bera du eta azkenarekin aldera daiteke. Hau, berriz, miaketa-zenbakitik eratorria zen, buruaren prezioan buztan-estaldura erosi zuena. 0 Aritmetikak seinalatzen zuen tokian hasi zen, materia gehien mugitzen zuen errenkadak, gutxi gora-behera, eta bi lasterketa ez ziren konparagarriak."

# libretranslate
msgid "``oidc-authenticator`` and ``ldap-authenticator`` are mutually exclusive auth backends (only one may be enabled; see ```tasks/01_validation.yml`` <./tasks/01_validation.yml>`__), each deriving its enablement from its bridged service flag. The OIDC/LDAP runtime configuration (provider URLs, bind DN, secrets) lives in the XWiki property templates and is read via ``lookup('config', application_id, 'secrets.credentials.<name>')``; the addon ``config:`` carries only the installer coordinate."
msgstr "``oidc-authenticator`` eta ``ldap-authenticator`` elkarren auth motor esklusiboak dira (bakarra gaitu daiteke; ikusi ```tasks/01_validation.yml`` <./tasks/01_validation.yml>`__), each deriving its enablement from its bridged service flag. The OIDC/LDAP runtime configuration (provider URLs, bind DN, secrets) lives in the XWiki property templates and is read via ``lookup('config', application_id, 'secrets.credentials.<name>')``; the addon ``config:`` Instalazioaren koordenatua bakarrik darama."

# libretranslate
msgid "``oidc``: baseline admin OIDC round-trip plus the three RBAC scenarios (subscriber/editor/administrator)."
msgstr "``oidc``: baseline admin OIDC marra biribila gehi RBAC agertokiak (subscriber/editor/administrator)."

# libretranslate
msgid "``openssl_conf_host`` (string): host path for generated openssl.cnf"
msgstr "``openssl_conf_host`` (katea): sortutako bide-izena openssl.cnf"

# libretranslate
msgid "``out`` itself lives under the dump dir (both derive from INFINITO_RESCUE_DIAGNOSTICS_DIR), so the walk must skip its own output subtree or copytree recurses into the growing destination until ENAMETOOLONG."
msgstr "``out`` Zabortegiaren azpian bizi da. (bietatik dator INFINITO_RESCUE_DIAGNOSTICS_DIR), Beraz, ibilaldiak bere irteerako azpizuhaitza saltatu behar du edo copytree-a gero eta handiagoa den helmugara itzuli behar du ENAMETOOLONG arte."

msgid "``owner/repo`` the branch lives on."
msgstr ""

# libretranslate
msgid "``owner/repo`` the run lives in."
msgstr "``owner/repo`` Korrika bizi da."

# libretranslate
msgid "``package.json`` and ``playwright.config.js`` are provided centrally by this role:"
msgstr "``package.json`` eta ``playwright.config.js`` Eginkizun honek zentralki hornitzen ditu:"

# libretranslate
msgid "``package_name`` (string) Name of the Python package to install (e.g., ``dockreap``, ``backup-docker-to-local``)."
msgstr "``package_name`` (katea) Instalatu beharreko Python paketearen izena (adibidez, ``dockreap``, ``backup-docker-to-local``)."

# libretranslate
msgid "``password`` (should come from vault/credentials)"
msgstr "``password`` (ganga edo kriedentials-etik etorri behar zuen)"

# libretranslate
msgid "``path``           the legacy ``path:`` field, ``''`` if absent"
msgstr "``path`` ondarea ``path:`` eremua, ``''`` baldin badago"

# libretranslate
msgid "``phpunit/phpunit`` declares ``_PHPUNIT_EXTENSIONS`` as platform requirements and Composer refuses to resolve the vendor tree without them, so they are part of the toolchain rather than of the suite consuming it. A distro ships them as packages separate from the interpreter, which is why a present ``php`` binary does not imply they are there."
msgstr "``phpunit/phpunit`` adierazten du ``_PHPUNIT_EXTENSIONS`` Plataformaren eskakizunek eta Composer-ek saltzailearen zuhaitza haiek gabe konpontzeari uko egiten diotenez, tresna-katearen parte dira, eta ez suitea. Distro batek pakete gisa bidaltzen ditu interpretatzailetik aparte, horregatik opari bat ``php`` Bitarrak ez du esan nahi hor daudenik."

msgid "``playwright.spec.js`` — orchestrator: TLS baseline, project creation, image asset upload, and the ``guest``/``biber``/``administrator`` personas. The ``biber`` / ``administrator`` personas are declared blocked via ``PERSONA_*_BLOCKED`` (mirroring ``web-app-taiga``): Penpot’s in-app “OpenID” entry and SPA user-menu logout aren’t driveable by the generic persona helper, so both users’ real auth is exercised by the dedicated login companions above."
msgstr ""

# libretranslate
msgid "``playwright.version`` in ``meta/services.yml`` is the single source of truth for the default Playwright version; the central ``templates/package.json.j2`` pins it via the ``image_version`` filter."
msgstr "``playwright.version`` barruan ``meta/services.yml`` Playwright bertsio lehenetsiaren egiaren iturri bakarra da; erdikoa ``templates/package.json.j2`` pins bidez ``image_version`` iragazkia."

# libretranslate
msgid "``plg_system_keycloak`` is built imperatively inside the Joomla container and speaks OIDC against Keycloak. Its enablement derives directly from the ``sso`` service flag, and its OIDC runtime contract (issuer, client id/secret, redirect/end-session URLs, fallback toggle, and RBAC group paths) lives under the addon’s ``config:`` block, which ```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__ renders into the ``JOOMLA_OIDC_*`` plugin environment."
msgstr "``plg_system_keycloak`` beharrezkoa da barruan Joomla edukiontzia eta hitz egiten du OIDCren aurka Keycloak. Bere ahalbidea zuzenean irteten da ``sso`` Zerbitzuaren bandera eta OIDCren iraupen-kontratua (jaulkitzailea, bezeroaren id/sekretua, birbideratzea/amaiera-saioaren URLak, atzera egitea eta RBAC taldearen bide-izenak) addonaren azpian bizi dira ``config:`` blokea, zein ```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__ renders into the ``JOOMLA_OIDC_*`` Pluginen ingurunea."

# libretranslate
msgid "``poll: 0`` makes a task fire and forget, so its own ``changed_when`` and ``failed_when`` never see an outcome. The outcome only exists once the job is collected with ``async_status``, and collecting it is where the verdict has to be made -- for a whole batch at once, so one run reports every broken job rather than the first."
msgstr "``poll: 0`` zeregin bat su egitea eta ahaztea, beraz, berea ``changed_when`` eta ``failed_when`` Ez da inoiz emaitzarik ikusten. Emaitza lana jasotzen denean bakarrik existitzen da. ``async_status``, eta bertan bildu behar da epaia, batch oso batentzat aldi berean, beraz, exekuzio batek lan hautsi guztiak berri ematen ditu, ez lehena."

# libretranslate
msgid "``ports.onion`` is a category-keyed map of booleans alongside ``internal`` / ``local`` / ``public``: it names which of a service's already-declared ports should answer on the node onion, and nothing else. The port number comes from ``ports.local`` when that category is declared there and from ``ports.public`` otherwise, which is the precedence ``container_ports`` publishes by, so the forward always targets the port the service is actually reachable on."
msgstr "``ports.onion`` kategoria-gakodun mapa bat da, boolearrekin batera ``internal`` / ``local`` / ``public``: Zerbitzu batek jadanik izendaturiko portuetatik zeini erantzun behar dion nodo-onionean, eta ez beste ezer. Ataka zenbakia hortik dator ``ports.local`` kategoria hori adierazten denean eta ``ports.public`` bestela, hori da lehentasuna ``container_ports`` argitaratzen du, eta, beraz, aurrera egiten du beti zerbitzua benetan eskura daitekeen portura."

# libretranslate
msgid "``priority`` IS the retrigger: it names what failed. ``offset`` is recomputed rather than carried, but from the carried value up: the source run got a stretch behind its own offset green before its budget ran out, so the regular line resumes behind that stretch (:func:`cli.administration.deploy.ci.selections.resume_offset`) instead of repeating it, and never falls back behind where that run started. Everything else is carried verbatim, including ``whitelist``, so a retrigger of a scoped run stays inside that scope instead of quietly widening to the whole repository."
msgstr "``priority`` Erredaktorea da, huts egin zuena izendatzen du. ``offset`` Ez da birkonputatua, baina egindako balioaren arabera: iturburu-exekuzioak tarte bat du bere offset berdearen atzean, aurrekontua amaitu baino lehen; beraz, lerro erregularra berriro hasten da tarte horren atzean. (:func:`cli.administration.deploy.ci.selections.resume_offset`) errepikatu ordez, eta inoiz ez da atzera egiten hasi zen lekura. Beste guztia literala da, baita ``whitelist``, Beraz, esparru horretan jarraitzen du, biltegi osoa lasai zabaldu beharrean."

# libretranslate
msgid "``provider`` / ``provider_key``: for ``onion_sso``, the app whose"
msgstr "``provider`` / ``provider_key``: ``onion_sso``, aplikazioa"

# libretranslate
msgid "``provides`` matching runs in both directions, so a provider (e.g. openldap ``provides: ldap``) is picked up even when the consuming flag uses a ``groups[...]`` form the ``group_names`` regex cannot read."
msgstr "``provides`` bat datozen bi norabideetan, beraz, hornitzaile bat (adibidez, irekia. ``provides: ldap``) Bandera kontsumitzen denean ere jasotzen da. ``groups[...]`` forma ``group_names`` regex-ek ezin du irakurri."

# libretranslate
msgid "``proxy_aliases``: aliases the beacon exposes for harvesting; falls back"
msgstr "``proxy_aliases``: beacon-a ezizenak biltzen ditu; erori egiten da"

# libretranslate
msgid "``proxy_pass`` directive; swarm prepends a ``set`` line (request-time DNS)."
msgstr "``proxy_pass`` direktiba; multzoka a ``set`` lerroa (DNS eskaera-denbora)."

# libretranslate
msgid "``proxy_resolvable``: beacon flag - the harvested aliases get attached to"
msgstr "``proxy_resolvable``: beacon bandera - bildutako aliasak erantsi egiten zaizkio"

# libretranslate
msgid "``quay.io/centos/centos:latest`` becomes ``centos:latest``; a two-segment image such as ``debian:13`` is returned unchanged."
msgstr "``quay.io/centos/centos:latest`` bihurtzen da ``centos:latest``; bi segmentuko irudi bat, adibidez ``debian:13`` aldatu gabe itzuli da."

# libretranslate
msgid "``reason``:          why a non-deployable classification cannot serve."
msgstr "``reason``-Zergatik ezin da sailkapena erabili."

# libretranslate
msgid "``relay`` and ``media`` are UDP. ``stun_turn`` and its TLS variant do speak TCP, but the allocation they hand out is a UDP relay address the onion client can never receive on, so forwarding the signalling port buys nothing."
msgstr "``relay`` eta ``media`` UDP dira. ``stun_turn`` eta bere TLS aldaerak TCP hitz egiten du, baina ematen duten esleipena UDP errelebo bat da, onion bezeroak inoiz jaso ezin duen helbidea, seinaleztapen-portua birbidaltzeak ez du ezer erosten."

# libretranslate
msgid "``repo`` carries the repository the names come from, defined inline on the entry that needs it: a full definition (``name``/``description``/ ``baseurl``/``gpgkey``) rendered as a yum repo, ``bootstrap_package`` for a repo shipped as a package such as ``epel-release``, ``enable_existing`` to switch on a repo the distro already ships, ``pacman_section`` to uncomment a section of ``pacman.conf`` such as ``multilib``, ``copr``/``ppa`` for a community repository, or ``managed_externally`` when the role sets it up itself."
msgstr "``repo`` Biltegia eramaten du, izenak behar duen sarreraren barnean definituta: definizio osoa (``name``/``description``/ ``baseurl``/``gpgkey``) yum repo bat bezala errea, ``bootstrap_package`` pakete bat bezala bidalia, ``epel-release``, ``enable_existing`` desbiderapen bat egiteko, jadanik itsasontziak zeuden, ``pacman_section`` atal bat desegitea ``pacman.conf`` adibidez ``multilib``, ``copr``/``ppa`` biltegi komunitario baterako, edo ``managed_externally`` rolak bere burua ezartzen duenean."

# libretranslate
msgid "``required`` (always installed)"
msgstr "``required`` (beti instalatuta)"

# libretranslate
msgid "``required`` (always installed, vendored)"
msgstr "``required`` (beti instalatuta, salduta)"

# libretranslate
msgid "``requirepass`` for the ``default`` (admin) user, sourced from the ``REDIS_PASSWORD`` credential."
msgstr "``requirepass`` zeren eta ``default`` (admin) erabiltzailea, hortik sortua ``REDIS_PASSWORD`` kredentziala."

# libretranslate
msgid "``retries`` counts CONSECUTIVE failures, and a request that leaves the container is load balanced across the service VIP. With N replicas and one of them alive, a round robin never produces more than N-1 failures in a row, so a streak based check is arithmetically blind to losing all but one backend. Chaining ``samples`` requests into a single probe makes one probe cover the whole pool instead."
msgstr "``retries`` CONSECUTIVE hutsegiteak zenbatzen ditu, eta edukiontzia uzten duen eskaera bat orekan dago zerbitzuaren VIP aldean. N erreplikak eta horietako bat bizirik daudelarik, lapur borobil batek ez du inoiz N baino gehiago sortzen...1 errenkada bateko hutsegiteak, beraz, marran oinarritutako txekea aritmetikoki itsua da motor bat besterik ez galtzeko. Kateatzea ``samples`` zunda bakar baten eskaerak igerileku osoa estaltzen du."

# libretranslate
msgid "``role`` may be a role name (relative to ``roles/``) or an absolute path to a role directory. Pass ``role_name`` explicitly when ``role`` is an arbitrary path whose basename is not the canonical role name."
msgstr "``role`` rol-izen bat izan daiteke (erlatiboa ``roles/``) edo funtzio-direktorio baterako bide absolutua. Pasatu ``role_name`` esplizitua: ``role`` Bide arbitrario bat da, zeinaren oinarri-izena ez den rol-izen kanonikoa."

# libretranslate
msgid "``roles/<app>/meta/server.yml`` declares ``status_codes`` keyed like ``domains.canonical``; it is the single source of truth for every prober."
msgstr "``roles/<app>/meta/server.yml`` adierazten du ``status_codes`` honela gakoa ``domains.canonical``; Egiaren iturri bakarra da prober guztientzat."

# libretranslate
msgid "``roles/<application_id>/files/playwright/playwright.spec.js`` Follow `Contributing ``playwright.env.j2`` <../../docs/agents/files/role/playwright.env.j2.md>`__ and `Contributing ``playwright.spec.js`` <../../docs/contributing/artefact/files/role/playwright.specs.js.md>`__ while creating them."
msgstr "``roles/<application_id>/files/playwright/playwright.spec.js`` Jarraitu `Contributing ``playwright.env.j2`` <../../docs/agents/files/role/playwright.env.j2.md>`__ eta `Contributing ``playwright.spec.js`` <../../docs/contributing/artefact/files/role/playwright.specs.js.md>`__ sortzen dituzten bitartean."

# libretranslate
msgid "``roles/sys-lint/meta/services.yml`` is the SPOT for both the repository and the version of every GitHub-release lint tool. Each entry carries the ``repository`` / ``ref`` pair that ``utils.update.repository`` already scans, so the existing ``update-repository-refs`` CI job bumps the pins to the latest semver tag and opens a PR -- the same machinery that keeps ``roles/pkgmgr`` current."
msgstr "``roles/sys-lint/meta/services.yml`` SPOT da biltegirako eta GitHub-en bertsiorako. Sarrera bakoitzak eramaten du ``repository`` / ``ref`` parea ``utils.update.repository`` jadanik eskaneatzen da, beraz, existitzen dena ``update-repository-refs`` CIk pinak azken semver etiketara jotzen ditu eta PR bat irekitzen du - makineria bera mantentzen duena ``roles/pkgmgr`` korrontea."

# libretranslate
msgid "``roles/test-e2e-playwright/files/playwright.config.js`` (copied as-is)"
msgstr "``roles/test-e2e-playwright/files/playwright.config.js`` (honela kopiatua)"

# libretranslate
msgid "``roles/test-e2e-playwright/templates/package.json.j2`` (rendered per-deploy; pins ``@playwright/test`` from ``meta/services.yml.playwright.version``)"
msgstr "``roles/test-e2e-playwright/templates/package.json.j2`` (bihurtuta; pinak ``@playwright/test`` - ``meta/services.yml.playwright.version``)"

# libretranslate
msgid "``roles_with_service('mcp', direction='server')`` entries."
msgstr "``roles_with_service('mcp', direction='server')`` sarrerak."

# libretranslate
msgid "``run_after``  — project-specific role-load-order list."
msgstr "``run_after`` - proiektu zehatzen zerrenda."

# libretranslate
msgid "``run_after`` is deliberately NOT read: it is a deploy-ordering hint, not a runtime dependency. The wider cosmos (federation peers, external bridged networks) cannot be derived from metadata and is left for the author to add."
msgstr "``run_after`` Ez da nahita irakurtzen: ordena-aholku bat da, ez iraupen-mendekotasun bat. Kosmos zabalagoa (Federazioko kideak, kanpoko sare zubiak) Ezin da metadatuetatik eratorri eta egileak gehitu behar du."

# libretranslate
msgid "``scripts/lint/packages.sh`` validates the generated packaging metadata with each ecosystem's native parser. This installer provisions those parsers wherever the platform's package manager can: on Debian (apt) the lint container gets ``dpkg-parsechangelog`` (``dpkg-dev``), ``rpmspec`` (``rpm``) and ``rpmlint``; on Arch (pacman) a dev host gets ``namcap``."
msgstr "``scripts/lint/packages.sh`` Sortutako paketatze-datuak balioztatzen ditu ekosistema bakoitzaren jatorrizko analizatzailearekin. Instalazio honek analizatzaile horiek hornitzen ditu plataformako pakete-kudeatzaileak ahal duen guztietan: Debianen (apt) lint edukiontzia lortzen du ``dpkg-parsechangelog`` (``dpkg-dev``), ``rpmspec`` (``rpm``) eta ``rpmlint``; Archen (pacman) ostalari batek hartzen du ``namcap``."

# libretranslate
msgid "``semantic_name``  the YAML key from ``meta/volumes.yml``"
msgstr "``semantic_name`` YAML gakoa ``meta/volumes.yml``"

# libretranslate
msgid "``services.<provider_key>.enabled`` must also hold. Default provider_key ``tor``"
msgstr "``services.<provider_key>.enabled`` Eutsi egin behar zaio. Lehenetsia provider_key ``tor``"

msgid "``services.code.flavor`` picks one of ``code-oss``, ``vscodium`` or ``vscode``. The three builds conflict at package level, so the role removes the other two before installing the chosen one."
msgstr ""

# libretranslate
msgid "``services.libretranslate``: image and version"
msgstr "``services.libretranslate``: irudia eta bertsioa"

msgid "``services.litellm.remote_models`` already narrowed to the providers this host holds a key for. An entry whose provider is ``mock`` answers from its own ``response`` and calls nothing."
msgstr ""

# libretranslate
msgid "``services.matomo``: enable analytics"
msgstr "``services.matomo``: gaitu analitika"

# libretranslate
msgid "``services.matrix.conferencing.element_call`` and ``services.matrix.conferencing.jitsi`` toggle MDAD’s Element Call / Jitsi stacks (ansible flavor only). Both default to true."
msgstr "``services.matrix.conferencing.element_call`` eta ``services.matrix.conferencing.jitsi`` toggle the Element Call / Jitsi pilak (zapore jangarria soilik). Biak lehenetsi egia."

msgid "``services.openwebui.embedding_model``, ``.image_model``, ``.speech_to_text_model`` and ``.text_to_speech_model`` route embeddings, images, speech recognition and speech synthesis through the gateway; an embedding model set here also replaces the sentence-transformer the image otherwise downloads from Hugging Face on first start"
msgstr ""

# libretranslate
msgid "``services.redis``: enable Redis backend"
msgstr "``services.redis``: Redis motorra"

msgid "``services.s1.flavor`` selects which implementation answers that contract. ``laya`` runs `Laya <https://huggingface.co/convaiinnovations/laya>`__, the default; ``torch`` and ``onnx`` run `jeff <https://github.com/logan-markewich/jeff>`__ over a GLiFormer encoder, which is what the role carried before. Neither upstream ships a container image, so the role builds one and bakes the checkpoints into it. Baking keeps the deploy free of a download at container start, which is the failure mode a sibling role’s model pull already hit."
msgstr ""

# libretranslate
msgid "``services.volume-2-local.snapshot_mode`` (declared in ``meta/services.yml``, overridable per host from the inventory) decides whether a run uses baudolo’s ``--snapshot`` mode. **Quote the value** — YAML reads a bare ``off``/``no``/``false`` as a boolean, and the deploy asserts on the result."
msgstr "``services.volume-2-local.snapshot_mode`` (deklaratuta ``meta/services.yml``, Inbentarioko ostalari bakoitzeko oso gomendagarria) Korrika batek baudoloren bat erabiltzen duen ala ez erabakitzen du. ``--snapshot`` modua. **Aipatu balioa** - YAMLk hutsa irakurtzen du ``off``/``no``/``false`` boolear gisa, eta deployak emaitza baieztatzen du."

# libretranslate
msgid "``set hostname to {{ inventory_hostname }}`` Applies the desired hostname."
msgstr "``set hostname to {{ inventory_hostname }}`` Nahi den ostalari-izena aplikatzen du."

# libretranslate
msgid "``setdefault`` falls back to the supplied value only when the process env has no non-empty value for the key. ``set`` is unconditional. ``get`` reads from the builder, falling back to the process env so derived values (e.g. ``INFINITO_CONTAINER``) can be composed off previously-set keys."
