# libretranslate
msgid "`auth_subject: administrator`: Home Assistant scopes the token to the account that minted it. This deployment mints it for the administrator, so a call arrives as the administrator whoever asked the client. Entity exposure still bounds the reach. Getting to the tool server is gated on the role's `mcp` RBAC group."
msgstr "`auth_subject: administrator`-Etxeko laguntzaileak tokena ezartzen du. Hedapen honek administratzaileari eragiten dio, eta dei bat iristen da bezeroari galdetu zion administratzaileari. Entitatearen esposizioak oraindik irismena mugatzen du. Tresna-zerbitzarira iristea rolean dago. `mcp` RBAC taldea."

# libretranslate
msgid "`auth_subject: administrator`: Mattermost bounds a call by the account the token belongs to. This deployment mints that personal access token for the administrator account, so calls arrive with that account's rights whoever asked. Reaching the tool server is gated on the role's `mcp` RBAC group."
msgstr "`auth_subject: administrator`-Batez ere, tokenaren kontuko dei bat mugatzen du. Hedapen honek administratzailearen konturako sarbide pertsonalaren tokena metatzen du, beraz, deiak kontu horren eskubideekin iristen dira, nork eskatu. Tresna-zerbitzarira iristean, paperaren gainean jartzen da. `mcp` RBAC taldea."

# libretranslate
msgid "`auth_subject: administrator`: the API token is issued against the administrator account, so every call carries that account's rights no matter who asked the client. Reaching the tool server is gated on the role's `mcp` RBAC group, which is a separate grant from administering Jenkins."
msgstr "`auth_subject: administrator`: API tokena administratzaile-kontuaren aurka igortzen da, beraz, dei bakoitzak kontu horren eskubideak ditu, bezeroak galdetuta ere. Tresna-zerbitzarira iristean, paperaren gainean jartzen da. `mcp` RBAC taldea, administraziotik aparte ematen dena Jenkins."

# libretranslate
msgid "`auth_subject: administrator`: the personal access token is minted against the `root` account and stored under the `administrator` key, so every call carries that account's rights no matter who asked the client. Reaching the tool server is gated on the role's `mcp` RBAC group, which is a separate grant from administering GitLab."
msgstr "`auth_subject: administrator`: sarbide pertsonalaren tokena miazkatzen da `root` kontua eta gordea `administrator` Gakoa, beraz, dei bakoitzak kontu horren eskubideak ditu, bezeroak galdetutakoa edozein dela ere. Tresna-zerbitzarira iristean, paperaren gainean jartzen da. `mcp` RBAC taldea, administraziotik aparte ematen dena GitLab."

# libretranslate
msgid "`auth_subject: administrator`: the web-service token is issued against the administrator account, so a call carries that account's rights regardless of who asked the client. The attached functions are read-only, which bounds what those rights can do here. Reaching the tool server is gated on the role's `mcp` RBAC group."
msgstr "`auth_subject: administrator`: web-zerbitzuaren tokena administratzailearen kontutik bidaltzen da, beraz, dei batek kontu horren eskubideak ditu, bezeroari nork eskatu dion kontuan hartu gabe. Erantsitako funtzioak irakurtzeko soilik dira, eta horrek mugatzen du eskubide horiek zer egin dezaketen hemen. Tresna-zerbitzarira iristean, paperaren gainean jartzen da. `mcp` RBAC taldea."

# libretranslate
msgid "`auth_subject: service_account | administrator` requires an explicit `tools.mutating_tools_enabled: false`."
msgstr "`auth_subject: service_account | administrator` esplizitua behar du `tools.mutating_tools_enabled: false`."

# libretranslate
msgid "`auth_subject: service_account`. A call arrives at Baserow as the endpoint owner regardless of who asked the client, and reaches only the one workspace that account owns. That is the second bound under the adapter's allowlist, not a substitute for it."
msgstr "`auth_subject: service_account`. Dei bat iristen da Baserow azken puntuaren jabea bezeroari galdetu ziona kontuan hartu gabe, eta kontua duen laneko area bakarra iristen da. Egokitzailearen baimen-zerrendako bigarren muga da, ez ordezkoa."

# libretranslate
msgid "`auth_subject: service_account`: [`tasks/utils/mcp/token.yml`](./tasks/utils/mcp/token.yml) creates the account `NEXTCLOUD_MCP_USERNAME` with `occ user:add` if it is missing, mints the app password against that account, and stores it under `mcp.credential.owner`. Every call carries that account's rights, not the administrator's, no matter who asked the client. Reaching the tool server is gated on the role's `mcp` RBAC group, which is a separate grant from holding a Nextcloud account."
msgstr "`auth_subject: service_account`: [`tasks/utils/mcp/token.yml`](./tasks/utils/mcp/token.yml) kontua sortzen du `NEXTCLOUD_MCP_USERNAME` honekin: `occ user:add` falta bada, aplikazioaren pasahitza kontu horren aurka txikitu eta azpian gordetzen du. `mcp.credential.owner`. Dei bakoitzak kontu horren eskubideak ditu, ez administratzailearenak, ez bezeroarenak. Tresna-zerbitzarira iristean, paperaren gainean jartzen da. `mcp` RBAC taldea, aparteko diru-laguntza da, eta Nextcloud kontua."

# libretranslate
msgid "`auth_subject: user` and `auth: oidc` claim that an MCP call executes with the requesting end user's permissions. A `delegation:` block records the audit that backs the claim; without it, [`test_mcp_schema.py`](../../../../../../tests/lint/ansible/services/test_mcp_schema.py) rejects the role."
msgstr "`auth_subject: user` eta `auth: oidc` MCP dei bat exekutatzen dela eskatzen duen azken erabiltzailearen baimenekin. A `delegation:` Blokeak erreklamazioaren atzera egiten duen auditoria erregistratzen du; hura gabe, [`test_mcp_schema.py`](../../../../../../tests/lint/ansible/services/test_mcp_schema.py) Rolari uko egiten dio."

# libretranslate
msgid "`auth_subject: user` or `auth: oidc` requires a `delegation` block; see [delegation.md](mcp/delegation.md)."
msgstr "`auth_subject: user` edo `auth: oidc` behar da `delegation` blokea; ikusi [delegation.md](mcp/delegation.md)."

